{"abstract":"We provide a formal modeling language, DACEO, for declarative asynchronous choreographies with general data-dependent message ordering and data objects. The language is equipped with execution semantics, and thereby, it can be used to specify the semantic and support monitoring of asynchronous distributed event-based systems in which a total ordering of message delivery cannot be assumed. DACEO models are graphs, which extends previous work on synchronous declarative choreographies based on Dynamic Condition Response Graphs and their operational semantics by adding asynchronous message channels with general data-dependent ordering constraints as well as general objects and data activities. The addition of objects builds on recent work on object-centric Dynamic Condition Response Graphs. We show that the DACEO Graphs can be encoded as the more basic Synchronous Object-centric Dynamic Condition Response Choreographies, preserving the semantics. We motivate DACEO by demonstrating its applicability in describing data-dependent ordering constraints between messages using a running example that shows how a system with causal consistency requirements can be specified. The marketplace is built on a benchmark for microservices that relies on asynchronous, event-based communication.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Zuckmantel, Tilman","Zhou, Yongluan","Düdder, Boris","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828470"],"event":{"end":"2025-06-19","place":"Lille, fr","start":"2025-06-17","title":"27th IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference on Coordination Models and Languages, COORDINATION 2025, Held as Part of the 20th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques, DisCoTec 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Event based systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"daceo declarative asynchronous choreographies with general data dependent event ordering and objects","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-828470","identifier":[{"id":"105009410831","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1f83c2ff-9dd6-4306-a400-72ec8a6c72aa"],"keyword":["Declarative Asynchronous Choreographies","Event-Based Systems","Formal Modeling Language","Message Ordering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F9305C4F2F93320E6F3B0B9C7A3E8ACD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tilman","key":"zuckmantelpau","last":"Zuckmantel","locid":"e8c41932-5eb8-478e-b1c3-149a62e74d1c","name":"Zuckmantel, Tilman","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yongluan","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"1df964e4-bf9e-48a1-a965-d33c6515c0bb","name":"Zhou, Yongluan","orcid":"0000-0002-7578-8117","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Boris","key":"düdderpau","last":"Düdder","locid":"26641b70-8c76-4150-ae85-086cfa904763","name":"Düdder, Boris","orcid":"0000-0002-0241-7729","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cinzia","key":"digiustopedh","last":"Di Giusto","name":"Di Giusto, Cinzia","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"António","key":"ravarapedh","last":"Ravara","name":"Ravara, António","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-95589-1_10","isbn":["9783031955884"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"197-216","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Coordination Models and Languages - 27th IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference, COORDINATION 2025, Held as Part of the 20th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques, DisCoTec 2025, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009410831"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1f83c2ff-9dd6-4306-a400-72ec8a6c72aa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DACEO : Declarative Asynchronous Choreographies with General Data-Dependent Event-Ordering and Objects","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828470","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This position paper introduces our view on a research agenda around human-centric hybrid-AI for reliable and explainable model-driven software engineering in the field of end-user, no-code development of process-aware information systems. Our key hypothesis is that reliable no-code development of such systems can be provided by using a hybrid-AI approach combining generative AI with explainable symbolic AI models through an intermediate formal, yet human-centric and understandable domain-specific language for the specification of behavioral scenarios.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Silva, Thiago Rocha","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-829813"],"event":{"end":"2025-06-27","place":"Trondheim, no","start":"2025-06-23","title":"33rd ACM International Conference on the Foundations of Software Engineering, FSE Companion 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["End User Development","Generative AI","Large Language Models","Model Driven Engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"human centric hybrid ai for no code development","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3696630.3731669","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-829813","identifier":[{"id":"105013966199","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c28c7ba0-d731-4e1a-88ff-9469d9540df2"],"keyword":["End-User Development","Generative AI","Large Language Models","Model-Driven Engineering","No-Code Development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-EBD19F80C2E20AC435A3760532FFABFB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3696630.3731669","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/463566239/Human-Centric_Hybrid-AI.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Thiago Rocha","key":"silvapau","last":"Silva","name":"Silva, Thiago Rocha","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas Troels","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas Troels","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jingyue","key":"lipedh","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jingyue","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3696630.3731669","eisbn":["9798400712760"],"issn":["15397521"],"pages":"1520-1521","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Proceedings of the ACM SIGSOFT Symposium on the Foundations of Software Engineering","status":"p","title":"FSE Companion 2025 - Companion Proceedings of the 33rd ACM International Conference on the Foundations of Software Engineering"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105013966199"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c28c7ba0-d731-4e1a-88ff-9469d9540df2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Human-Centric Hybrid-AI for No-Code Development","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-829813","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Venous thromboembolism (VTE) is a frequent complication in critically ill patients, who often have multiple risk factors. Pharmacological thromboprophylaxis is widely applied to lower this risk, but guidelines lack dosing recommendations. OBJECTIVE: This survey aims to assess current thromboprophylaxis preferences and willingness to participate in future randomized clinical trials (RCTs) on this topic. METHOD: We conducted an international online survey between February and May 2023 among intensive care unit (ICU) physicians, including 16 questions about preferences in relation to thromboprophylaxis and preferences on topics for a future RCT. The survey was distributed through the network of the Collaboration for Research in Intensive Care. RESULTS: A total of 715 physicians from 170 ICUs in 23 countries contributed information, with a mean response rate of 36%. In most ICUs, both pharmacological (n = 166, 98%) and mechanical thromboprophylaxis (n = 143, 84%) were applied. A total of 36 pharmacological thromboprophylaxis regimens were reported. Use of low-molecular-weight heparin (LMWH) was most common (n = 149 ICUs, 87%), followed by subcutaneous unfractionated heparin (n = 44 ICUs, 26%). Seventy-five percent of physicians indicated that they used enoxaparin 40 mg (4000 IU), dalteparin 5000 IU, or tinzaparin 4500 IU once daily, whereas 25% reported the use of 16 other LMWH type and dose combinations. Dose adjustment according to weight was common (78 ICUs, 46%). Participants perceived high variation in the application of thromboprophylaxis and were willing to consider an alternative LMWH type (n = 542, 76%) or dose (n = 538, 75%) in the context of an RCT. CONCLUSION: LMWH was the preferred agent for thromboprophylaxis in critically ill patients. There was considerable variation in the application of LMWH for prophylaxis, reflected by the use of different types, doses, and dosing strategies. Most physicians would be willing to participate in an RCT on thromboprophylaxis. EDITORIAL COMMENT: This survey demonstrates current patterns in implementation preferences for critically ill patients. While there is one approach and drug that is commonly preferred, these findings show that there is some variation in practice.","author_count":55,"contributors":["Heijkoop, Èmese Robin Hélène","Keus, Frederik","Møller, Morten Hylander","Perner, Anders","Morgan, Matthew","Abdelhadi, Adel","Al Shirawi, Nehad Nabeel Mohamed","Al-Fares, Abdulrahman A.","Alshamsi, Fayez","Ananthan, Prakkash Parangi","Andreasen, Anne Sofie","Anstey, Matthew H.","Arabi, Yaseen M.","Aslam, Tayyba Naz","Attokaran, Antony George","Bestle, Morten H.","Bhadange, Neeraj","Blaser, Annika Reintam","Brøchner, Anne Craveiro","Cronhjort, Maria","Dąbrowski, Wojciech","Elhoufi, Ashraf","Ergan, Begum","Ferrer, Ricard","Freebairn, Ross","Fujii, Tomoko","Greco, Massimiliano","van Haren, Frank M.P.","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Hjortrup, Peter Buhl","Ho, Kwok M.","Jonmarker, Sandra","Kruger, Peter","Malbrain, Manu L.N.G.","Mallat, Jihad","Marella, Prashanti","Mer, Mervyn","Meyhoff, Tine Sylvest","Nalos, Marek","Nassef, Mohamed","Omar, Rania","Orde, Sam","Ostermann, Marlies","Pilcher, David","Poulsen, Lone Musaeus","Rai, Sumeet","Shekar, Kiran","Siegemund, Martin","Sigurdsson, Martin Ingi","Rasmussen, Bodil","Troelsen, Thomas Tværmose","Krag, Mette","Young, Paul","Meijer, Karina","Eck, Ruben Julius"],"cuid":["S03-085.54-803674"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Africa","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Heijkoop, Èmese Robin Hélène"],"country":["Australia","China","Czechia","Estonia","Hong Kong","Iceland","Italy","Japan","Kuwait","Netherlands","New Zealand","Norway","Poland","Saudi Arabia","South Africa","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","United Arab Emirates","United Kingdom"