{"abstract":"We present an approach to the proactive enforcement of provisions and obligations, suitable for building policy enforcement mechanisms that both prevent and cause system actions. Our approach encompasses abstract requirements for proactive policy enforcement, a system model describing how enforcement mechanisms interact with and control target systems, and concrete policy languages and associated enforcement mechanisms. As examples of policy languages, we consider finite automata and timed dynamic condition response (DCR) graphs. We use finite automata to illustrate the basic principles and DCR graphs to show how these principles can be adapted to a practical, real-time policy language. In both cases, we show how to algorithmically determine whether a given policy is enforceable and, when this is the case, construct an associated enforcement mechanism. Our approach improves upon existing formalisms in two ways: (1) we exploit the target system's existing functionality to avert policy violations proactively, rather than compensate for them reactively; and (2) rather than requiring the manual specification of remedial actions in the policy, we deduce required actions directly from the policy.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Basin, David","Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-749105"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ETH Zürich"],"keyword":["Access control","Business process modeling","Obligations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proactive enforcement of provisions and obligations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-749105","identifier":[{"id":"85196660902","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c6918be5-bde2-4b50-8876-1f3e2afb5ccb"],"keyword":["Access control","business process modeling","obligations","run-time enforcement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-98E72C012B118C306E2E0F03DA4354BE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"eth zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"ETH Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"David","key":"basinpau","last":"Basin","name":"Basin, David","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3233/jcs-210078","issn":["0926227X","18758924"],"issn_org":["0926227X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Computer Security","pages":"247-289","status":"p","title":"Journal of Computer Security","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196660902"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c6918be5-bde2-4b50-8876-1f3e2afb5ccb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Proactive enforcement of provisions and obligations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-749105","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Discovering simple, understandable and yet accurate process models is a well-known issue for models mined from real-life event logs. In this paper, we consider algorithms for automatically computing nested groups of activities in declarative process languages, concretely Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) Graphs, to reduce complexity while preserving accuracy. The DCR Graphs notation is, on the one hand, supported by the very accurate DisCoveR process mining algorithm, and on the other hand, by mature design and execution tools used in industrial processes and enterprise information management systems. We evaluate our approach by applying the DisCoveR miner to a large benchmark of real-life and synthetic event logs, measuring the size, density, separability, and constraint variability of mined models with and without grouping of activities. In earlier work, these measures have been shown to have a significant effect on the intrinsic cognitive load for users of declarative models, in particular DCR Graphs. We also evaluate the effect of prioritizing in particular the grouping of activities that model mutual exclusive choices. Our evaluation confirms that grouping of activities in general lowers the complexity on 3 of the 4 measures, while prioritizing choices in some cases makes the improvement slightly smaller.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Cosma, Vlad Paul","Christfort, Axel Kjeld Fjelrad","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Lu, Xixi","Reijers, Hajo A.","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-749142"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-07","place":"Limassol, cy","start":"2024-06-03","title":"36th International Conference on Advanced Information Systems Engineering, CAiSE 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Choices","DCR Graphs","Declarative","Process discovery","Simplicity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving simplicity by discovering nested groups in declarative models","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-61057-8_26","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-749142","identifier":[{"id":"85196753558","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cb4d23dd-e940-4a3b-ac90-ccb072ea9f0a"],"keyword":["Choices","DCR Graphs","Declarative","Nested Groups","Process Discovery","Simplicity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49876E6EBFDC380B3FC8B1A10C721E17"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/397029247/Improving_Simplicity.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-61057-8_26","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Vlad Paul","key":"cosmapau","last":"Cosma","locid":"2e80a2e2-1e2e-49ee-933c-fe4a76cc2586","name":"Cosma, Vlad Paul","orcid":"0000-0001-8022-6402","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Axel Kjeld Fjelrad","key":"christfortpau","last":"Christfort","locid":"93296adf-650b-45c5-99fe-13923420b0f5","name":"Christfort, Axel Kjeld Fjelrad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Xixi","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Xixi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hajo A.","key":"reijerspau","last":"Reijers","name":"Reijers, Hajo A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Giancarlo","key":"guizzardipedh","last":"Guizzardi","name":"Guizzardi, Giancarlo","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Flavia","key":"santoropedh","last":"Santoro","name":"Santoro, Flavia","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Haralambos","key":"mouratidispedh","last":"Mouratidis","name":"Mouratidis, Haralambos","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Pnina","key":"sofferpedh","last":"Soffer","name":"Soffer, Pnina","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-61057-8_26","isbn":["9783031610561"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"440-455","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Advanced Information Systems Engineering - 36th International Conference, CAiSE 2024, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196753558"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cb4d23dd-e940-4a3b-ac90-ccb072ea9f0a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Improving Simplicity by Discovering Nested Groups in Declarative Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-749142","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Research question: Do platelet-rich plasma (PRP) products, specifically human platelet lysate (hPL) and umbilical cord plasma, enhance vascularization and follicular survival in human ovarian tissue transplanted to immunodeficient mice? Design: Human ovarian tissue was transplanted to subcutaneous pockets in nude mice, followed by daily injections for 6 days of PRP or saline at the transplantation sites. After a grafting period of 3 and 6 days, vascularization was assessed using CD-31 quantification, and gene expression of angiogenic markers (VEGF/Vegf) together with apoptosis-related genes (BAX/BCL-2), oxidative stress markers (HMOX-1/Hmox-1) and pro-inflammatory markers (Il-1β/Il-6/Tnf-α) was quantitively analysed. Follicle density was analysed in the grafts after 4 weeks. Additionally, a pilot study was conducted exploring the suitability of ultrasound scanning for assessing survival and vascularization in ovarian tissue xenografted to mice. Results: Although there was a significant increase in the CD-31 area from day 3 to day 6 post-grafting, there were no significant differences between the hPL and control groups. Gene expression analysis revealed significant down-regulation of VEGF from day 3 to day 6 for both the hPL and control groups, and significant up-regulation of BAX/BCL-2 in the hPL group compared with the controls. The follicle density showed no significant differences in the hPL group and UCP groups compared with the controls. Furthermore, ultrasound biomicroscopy provided valuable insights into graft morphology, necrotic areas and blood flow, suggesting its potential as a monitoring tool. Conclusions: Despite the angiogenic properties of PRP, this study was unable to demonstrate a significant impact of hPL on vascularization or of hPL and UCP on follicular survival in xenotransplanted human ovarian tissue.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Subiran Adrados, Cristina","Olesen, Hanna Ørnes","Olesen, Sophie Vernimmen","Pors, Susanne Elisabeth","Holtze, Sussanne","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Andersen, Claus Yding","Kristensen, Stine Gry"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-779429"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Free University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Follicles","Ovarian tissue cryopreservation","Ovarian tissue transplantation","Platelet Rich Plasma","Vascularization"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the effect of platelet rich plasma on vascularization and survival of follicles in xenotransplanted human ovarian tissue","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rbmo.2024.104274","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-779429","identifier":[{"id":"39146901","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85201160905","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-eec47755-dc94-4a7f-aee1-5531945060db"],"keyword":["Follicles","Ovarian tissue cryopreservation","Ovarian tissue transplantation","Platelet-rich plasma","Vascularization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-856FC7C71D9B1E87D715E31DC9F87912"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/413947185/Exploring_the_effect_of_platelet_rich_plasma_on_vascularization_and_survival_of_follicles_in_xenotransplanted_human_ovarian_tissue.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rbmo.2024.104274","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"free university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Free University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Cristina","key":"subiranadradoscristinapau","last":"Subiran Adrados","name":"Subiran Adrados, Cristina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanna Ørnes","key":"olesenhannaørnespau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Hanna Ørnes","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sophie Vernimmen","key":"olesensophievernimmenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Sophie Vernimmen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne Elisabeth","key":"porssusanneelisabethpau","last":"Pors","name":"Pors, Susanne Elisabeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sussanne","key":"holtzesussannepau","last":"Holtze","name":"Holtze, Sussanne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtthomaspau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Claus Yding","key":"andersenclausydingpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"de926ac7-21b1-4c38-8d85-3c8e45cd483a","name":"Andersen, Claus Yding","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stine Gry","key":"kristensenstinegrypau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Stine Gry","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39146901"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.rbmo.2024.104274","issn":["14726483","14726491"],"issn_org":["14726483"],"issue":"4","journal":"Reproductive BioMedicine Online","paperid":"104274","status":"p","title":"Reproductive BioMedicine Online","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201160905"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-eec47755-dc94-4a7f-aee1-5531945060db"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring the effect of platelet-rich plasma on vascularization and survival of follicles in xenotransplanted human ovarian tissue","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-779429","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Platelet transfusions are frequently used in the intensive care unit (ICU), but current practices including used product types, volumes, doses and effects are unknown. Study design and methods: Sub-study of the inception cohort study ‘Thrombocytopenia and Platelet Transfusions in the ICU (PLOT-ICU)’, including acutely admitted, adult ICU patients with thrombocytopenia (platelet count <150 × 109/L). The primary outcome was the number of patients receiving platelet transfusion in ICU by product type. Secondary outcomes included platelet transfusion details, platelet increments, bleeding, other transfusions and mortality. Results: Amongst 504 patients with thrombocytopenia from 43 hospitals in 10 countries in Europe and the United States, 20.8% received 565 platelet transfusions; 61.0% received pooled products, 21.9% received apheresis products and 17.1% received both with a median of 2 (interquartile range 1–4) days from admission to first transfusion. The median volume per transfusion was 253 mL (180–308 mL) and pooled products accounted for 59.1% of transfusions, however, this varied across countries. Most centres (73.8%) used fixed dosing (medians ranging from 2.0 to 3.5 × 1011 platelets/transfusion) whilst some (mainly in France) used weight-based dosing (ranging from 0.5 to 0.7 × 1011 platelets per 10 kg body weight). The median platelet count increment for a single prophylactic platelet transfusion was 2 (−1 to 8) × 109/L. Outcomes of patients with thrombocytopenia who did and did not receive platelet transfusions varied. Conclusions: Among acutely admitted, adult ICU patients with thrombocytopenia, 20.8% received platelet transfusions in ICU of whom most received pooled products, but considerable variation was observed in product type, volumes and doses across countries. Prophylactic platelet transfusions were associated with limited increases in platelet counts.","author_count":49,"contributors":["Anthon, Carl Thomas","Pène, Frédéric","Perner, Anders","Azoulay, Elie","Puxty, Kathryn","Van De Louw, Andry","Chawla, Sanjay","Castro, Pedro","Povoa, Pedro","Coelho, Luis","Metaxa, Victoria","Kochanek, Matthias","Liebregts, Tobias","Kander, Thomas","Sivula, Mirka","Andreasen, Jo Bønding","Nielsen, Lene Bjerregaard","Hvas, Christine Lodberg","Dufranc, Etienne","Canet, Emmanuel","Wright, Christopher John","Schmidt, Julien","Uhel, Fabrice","Missri, Louai","Krag, Mette","Cos Badia, Elisabet","Díaz-Lagares, Cándido","Menat, Sophie","Voiriot, Guillaume","Erikstrup Clausen, Niels","Lorentzen, Kristian","Kvåle, Reidar","Barratt-Due, Andreas","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Holten, Aleksander Rygh","Strand, Kristian","Bestle, Morten Heiberg","Klepstad, Pål","Vimpere, Damien","Paulino, Carolina","Lueck, Catherina","Juhl, Christian Svendsen","Costa, Carolina","Bådstøløkken, Per Martin","Lêdo, Lia Susana Aires","Møller, Morten Hylander","Russell, Lene"],"cuid":["S04-094.90-755898"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Anthon, Carl Thomas"],"country":["Australia","Finland","France","Germany","Norway","Portugal","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["AP-HP Assistance Publique - Hopitaux de Paris","Akershus University Hospital","All Global Affiliations","Assistance publique – Hôpitaux de Paris","Avicenne Hospital","CHU Nantes","CHU de Nantes","Centro Hospitalar de Lisboa Central","Centro Hospitalar de Lisboa Ocidental","Cornell University","EPE","Essen University Hospital","Glasgow Royal Infirmary","Hannover Medical School","Haukeland University Hospital","Helsinki University Hospital","Hopital Avicenne","Hopital Tenon","Hospital Clínic de Barcelona","Hospital Cochin","Hospital Fernando Fonseca","Hospital General Granollers","Hospital General de Granollers","Hospital Professor Doutor Fernando Fonseca","Hospita