{"abstract":"What information should and can be transparent for artificial intelligence (AI) algorithms? This article examines the socio- technical and legal perspectives of transparency in relation to algorithmic decision-making in public administration. We show how transparency in AI can be understood in light of the various technologies and the challenges one may encounter. Despite some first steps in that direction, there exists so far no mature standard for documenting AI models. From a legal perspective, this article examined the applicable freedom of information (FOI) regimes across different jurisdictions, with a particular focus on Denmark and other Scandinavian countries. Despite notable differences, our findings show that the FOI regimes generally only grant access to existing documents, and that access can be denied on the basis of the wide proprietary interests and internal documents exemptions. This is why we ultimately conclude that the European data-protection framework and the proposed EU AI Act -with their far-reaching duties to document the functioning of AI systems -provide promising new avenues for research and insights into transparency in AI.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Olsen, Henrik Palmer","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Wiesener, Cornelius","Larsen, Matthias Smed","Flügge, Asbjørn Ammitzbøll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-732653"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Algorithm","Transparency","freedom of information"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the right to transparency in public governance freedom of information and the use of artificial intelligence by public agencies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3632753","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-732653","identifier":[{"id":"85187807869","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e1be0e65-f781-469c-911e-89e446901939"],"keyword":["Transparency","administrative decision-making","algorithm","freedom of information"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3CE58E040343BE1D42B395E59CF0BD9C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/388020275/The_Right_to_Transparency.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3632753","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Law, Area of Research, Centre of Excellence for International Courts and Governance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Palmer","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"d6151186-5867-4059-bc35-8e82ae4be33e","name":"Olsen, Henrik Palmer","orcid":"0000-0001-8486-8752","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Troels","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas Troels","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cornelius","key":"wiesenerpau","last":"Wiesener","locid":"e51ee645-3ce8-41f9-b9a4-918882937c3f","name":"Wiesener, Cornelius","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias Smed","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Matthias Smed","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Asbjørn William","key":"ammitzbøllflüggepau","last":"Ammitzbøll Flügge","locid":"5924a30c-e320-4cf0-a5a2-226f7fc8f15e","name":"Flügge, Asbjørn Ammitzbøll","name_org":"Ammitzbøll Flügge, Asbjørn William","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3632753","issn":["26390175"],"issue":"1","journal":"Digital Government: Research and Practice","paperid":"8","status":"p","title":"Digital Government: Research and Practice","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85187807869"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e1be0e65-f781-469c-911e-89e446901939"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Right to Transparency in Public Governance : Freedom of Information and the Use of Artificial Intelligence by Public Agencies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-732653","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Logical flaws in smart contracts are often exploited, leading to significant financial losses. Our tool, HighGuard, detects transactions that violate business logic specifications of smart contracts. HighGuard employs dynamic condition response (DCR) graph models as formal specifications to verify contract execution against these models. It is capable of operating in a cross-chain environment for detecting business logic flaws across different blockchain platforms. We demonstrate HighGuard's effectiveness in identifying deviations from specified behaviors in smart contracts without requiring code instrumentation or incurring additional gas costs. By using precise specifications in the monitor, HighGuard achieves detection without false positives. Our evaluation, involving 54 exploits, confirms HighGuard's effectiveness in detecting business logic vulnerabilities.Our open-source implementation of HighGuard and a screencast of its usage are available at: https://github.com/mojtaba-eshghie/HighGuardhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZYVV-slDaY.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Eshghie, Mojtaba","Artho, Cyrille","Stammler, Hans","Ahrendt, Wolfgang","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Schneider, Gerardo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811328"],"event":{"end":"2024-11-01","place":"Sacramento, us","start":"2024-10-28","title":"39th ACM/IEEE International Conference on Automated Software Engineering, ASE 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Blockchain Security","DCR Graphs","Runtime monitoring","Smart contracts"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"highguard cross chain business logic monitoring of smart contracts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3691620.3695356","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-811328","identifier":[{"id":"85211650421","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e6a69594-00f3-4bdd-916c-75f7d933ce69"],"keyword":["DCR graphs","blockchain security","runtime monitoring","smart contracts"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-530E21FB4B4F57209D6743BA2432E367"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3691620.3695356","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/444872650/HighGuard.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mojtaba","key":"eshghiepau","last":"Eshghie","name":"Eshghie, Mojtaba","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cyrille","key":"arthopau","last":"Artho","name":"Artho, Cyrille","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans","key":"stammlerpau","last":"Stammler","name":"Stammler, Hans","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Wolfgang","key":"ahrendtpau","last":"Ahrendt","name":"Ahrendt, Wolfgang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Gerardo","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","name":"Schneider, Gerardo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3691620.3695356","eisbn":["9798400712487"],"pages":"2378-2381","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","status":"p","title":"Proceedings - 2024 39th ACM/IEEE International Conference on Automated Software Engineering, ASE 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211650421"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e6a69594-00f3-4bdd-916c-75f7d933ce69"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"HighGuard : Cross-Chain Business Logic Monitoring of Smart Contracts","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-811328","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"IMPORTANCE: Supplemental oxygen is ubiquitously used in patients with COVID-19 and severe hypoxemia, but a lower dose may be beneficial. OBJECTIVE: To assess the effects of targeting a Pao2 of 60 mm Hg vs 90 mm Hg in patients with COVID-19 and severe hypoxemia in the intensive care unit (ICU). DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS: Multicenter randomized clinical trial including 726 adults with COVID-19 receiving at least 10 L/min of oxygen or mechanical ventilation in 11 ICUs in Europe from August 2020 to March 2023. The trial was prematurely stopped prior to outcome assessment due to slow enrollment. End of 90-day follow-up was June 1, 2023. INTERVENTIONS: Patients were randomized 1:1 to a Pao2 of 60 mm Hg (lower oxygenation group; n = 365) or 90 mm Hg (higher oxygenation group; n = 361) for up to 90 days in the ICU. MAIN OUTCOMES AND MEASURES: The primary outcome was the number of days alive without life support (mechanical ventilation, circulatory support, or kidney replacement therapy) at 90 days. Secondary outcomes included mortality, proportion of patients with serious adverse events, and number of days alive and out of hospital, all at 90 days. RESULTS: Of 726 randomized patients, primary outcome data were available for 697 (351 in the lower oxygenation group and 346 in the higher oxygenation group). Median age was 66 years, and 495 patients (68%) were male. At 90 days, the median number of days alive without life support was 80.0 days (IQR, 9.0-89.0 days) in the lower oxygenation group and 72.0 days (IQR, 2.0-88.0 days) in the higher oxygenation group (P = .009 by van Elteren test; supplemental bootstrapped adjusted mean difference, 5.8 days [95% CI, 0.2-11.5 days]; P = .04). Mortality at 90 days was 30.2% in the lower oxygenation group and 34.7% in the higher oxygenation group (risk ratio, 0.86 [98.6% CI, 0.66-1.13]; P = .18). There were no statistically significant differences in proportion of patients with serious adverse events or in number of days alive and out of hospital. CONCLUSION AND RELEVANCE: In adult ICU patients with COVID-19 and severe hypoxemia, targeting a Pao2 of 60 mm Hg resulted in more days alive without life support in 90 days than targeting a Pao2 of 90 mm Hg. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT04425031.","author_count":53,"contributors":["Nielsen, Frederik M","Klitgaard, Thomas L","Siegemund, Martin","Laake, Jon H","Thormar, Katrin M","Cole, Jade M","Aagaard, Søren R","Bunzel, Anne-Marie G","Vestergaard, Stine R","Langhoff, Peter K","Pedersen, Caroline H","Hejlesen, Josefine Ø","Abdelhamid, Salim","Dietz, Anna","Gebhard, Caroline E","Zellweger, Nuria","Hollinger, Alexa","Poulsen, Lone M","Weihe, Sarah","Andersen-Ranberg, Nina C","Pedersen, Ulf G","Mathiesen, Ole","Andreasen, Anne Sofie","Brix, Helene","Thomsen, Jonas J","Petersen, Christina H","Bestle, Morten H","Wichmann, Sine","Lund, Martin S","Mortensen, Karoline M","Brand, Björn A","Haase, Nicolai","Iversen, Susanne A","Marcussen, Klaus V","Brøchner, Anne C","Borup, Morten","Grøfte, Thorbjørn","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Kjær, Maj-Brit N","Engstrøm, Janus","Lange, Theis","Perner, Anders","Schjørring, Olav L","Rasmussen, Bodil S"],"cuid":["S03-099.97-735023"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["HOT-COVID Trial Group"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Bodil S.","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen"],"country":["Iceland","Norway","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Landspitali University Hospital","Oslo University Hospital","The National University Hospital of Iceland","University Hospital Basel","University Hospital Wales","University Hospital of Basel","University Hospital of Wales"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","COVID 19 therapy","Female","Humans","Hypoxia etiology","Male","Oxygen","Oxygen Inhalation Therapy methods","Respiration Artificial"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Institute of Medical Genetics, University Hospital of Wales, Cardiff, UK."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lower vs higher oxygenation target and days alive without life support in covid 000000000019 the hot covid randomized clinical trial","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85189877590&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Conflict of Interest Disclosures: Dr Mathiesen reported contract research for AM Pharma and receipt of grants from Novo Nordisk Foundation for the RECIPE trial, grants from Sygeforsikringen Danmark for the PERISAFE trial, and grants from Independent Research Fund Denmark for the PERISAFE trial. Dr Wichmann reported receipt of grants from Novo Nordisk Foundation, Sygeforsikringen Danmark, Svend Andersen Foundation, and Ehrenreich Foundation. Dr Kj\\u00E6r reported receipt of grants from Novo Nordisk Foundation and Sygeforsikringen Danmark. Dr Lange reported receipt of personal fees from Novo Nordisk and Leo Pharma. Dr Perner reported receipt of grants from Novo Nordisk Foundation and Sygeforsikringen Danmark and personal fees from Novartis. Dr Rasmussen reported receipt of grants from Novo Nordisk Foundation. No other disclosures were reported. Funding/Support: The trial was funded by the Danish Ministry of Education and Science and supported by the Research Council at Aalborg University Hospital."],"id":"S03-099.97-735023","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10951852","type":"pmcid"},{"id"