"name":"Leibniz Institute for Zoo and Wildlife Research","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"fr","key":"montpellier university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Montpellier University","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"fr","key":"ird institut de recherche pour le developpement","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"IRD Institut de Recherche pour le Developpement","used":1},{"affno":"12","country":"de","key":"charité universitätsmedizin berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"13","country":"de","key":"museum für naturkunde leibniz institute for evolution and biodiversity science","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Museum für Naturkunde - Leibniz Institute for Evolution and Biodiversity Science","used":1},{"affno":"14","country":"mx","key":"instituto politécnico nacional","loc":["Mexico","America, Central","OECD"],"name":"Instituto Politécnico Nacional","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Korbinian","key":"pacherkorbinianpau","last":"Pacher","name":"Pacher, Korbinian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Michael","key":"breukermichaelpau","last":"Breuker","name":"Breuker, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthew J.","key":"hansenmatthewjpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Matthew J.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Ralf H.J.M.","key":"kurversralfhjmpau","last":"Kurvers","name":"Kurvers, Ralf H.J.M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Jan","key":"hägejanpau","last":"Häge","name":"Häge, Jan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Felicie","key":"dhellemmesfeliciepau","last":"Dhellemmes","name":"Dhellemmes, Felicie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Paolo","key":"domenicipaolopau","last":"Domenici","name":"Domenici, Paolo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"John F.","key":"steffensenjohnflengpau","last":"Steffensen","locid":"1c16bed2-acb3-4cc5-a09a-a2ab80939e53","name":"Steffensen, John Fleng","name_org":"Steffensen, John F.","orcid":"0000-0002-4477-8039","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Stefan","key":"krausestefanpau","last":"Krause","name":"Krause, Stefan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtthomaspau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Guido","key":"fritschguidopau","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Guido","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10 11","first":"Pascal","key":"bachpascalpau","last":"Bach","name":"Bach, Pascal","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10 11","first":"Philippe S.","key":"sabarrosphilippespau","last":"Sabarros","name":"Sabarros, Philippe S.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","first":"Paul","key":"zaslanskypaulpau","last":"Zaslansky","name":"Zaslansky, Paul","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","first":"Kristin","key":"mahlowkristinpau","last":"Mahlow","name":"Mahlow, Kristin","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","first":"Johannes","key":"müllerjohannespau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, Johannes","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"14","first":"Rogelio González","key":"armasrogeliogonzálezpau","last":"Armas","name":"Armas, Rogelio González","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"14","first":"Hector Villalobos","key":"ortizhectorvillalobospau","last":"Ortiz","name":"Ortiz, Hector Villalobos","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"14","first":"Felipe","key":"galvánmagañafelipepau","last":"Galván-Magaña","name":"Galván-Magaña, Felipe","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 5","first":"Jens","key":"krausejenspau","last":"Krause","name":"Krause, Jens","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37987173"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jfb.15608","issn":["00221112","10958649"],"issn_org":["00221112"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Fish Biology","pages":"713-722","status":"p","title":"Journal of Fish Biology","volume":"104"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178227219"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a2eb4e25-801b-4772-a3e1-18e8d450fd50"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The rostral micro-tooth morphology of blue marlin, <i>Makaira nigricans</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-731986","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We compared the image quality and quantification parameters through bayesian penalized likelihood reconstruction algorithm (Q.Clear) and ordered subset expectation maximization (OSEM) algorithm for 2-[ 18F]FDG-PET/CT scans performed for response monitoring in patients with metastatic breast cancer in prospective setting. We included 37 metastatic breast cancer patients diagnosed and monitored with 2-[ 18F]FDG-PET/CT at Odense University Hospital (Denmark). A total of 100 scans were analyzed blinded toward Q.Clear and OSEM reconstruction algorithms regarding image quality parameters (noise, sharpness, contrast, diagnostic confidence, artefacts, and blotchy appearance) using a five-point scale. The hottest lesion was selected in scans with measurable disease, considering the same volume of interest in both reconstruction methods. SUL peak (g/mL) and SUV max (g/mL) were compared for the same hottest lesion. There was no significant difference regarding noise, diagnostic confidence, and artefacts within reconstruction methods; Q.Clear had significantly better sharpness ( p < 0.001) and contrast ( p = 0.001) than the OSEM reconstruction, while the OSEM reconstruction had significantly less blotchy appearance compared with Q.Clear reconstruction ( p < 0.001). Quantitative analysis on 75/100 scans indicated that Q.Clear reconstruction had significantly higher SUL peak (5.33 ± 2.8 vs. 4.85 ± 2.5, p < 0.001) and SUV max (8.27 ± 4.8 vs. 6.90 ± 3.8, p < 0.001) compared with OSEM reconstruction. In conclusion, Q.Clear reconstruction revealed better sharpness, better contrast, higher SUV max, and higher SUL peak, while OSEM reconstruction had less blotchy appearance.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Naghavi-Behzad, Mohammad","Vogsen, Marianne","Gerke, Oke","Dahlsgaard-Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth","Nissen, Henriette Juel","Jakobsen, Nick Møldrup","Braad, Poul-Erik","Vilstrup, Mie Holm","Deak, Paul","Hildebrandt, Malene Grubbe","Andersen, Thomas Lund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-574727"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Naghavi-Behzad, Mohammad"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GE Healthcare"],"keyword":["FDG PET CT","Metastatic breast cancer","Reconstruction algorithm"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Department at Clinical Engineering, Region of Southern Denmark, 6200 Aabenraa, Denmark"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of image quality and quantification parameters between q clear and osem reconstruction methods on fdg pet ct images in patients with metastatic breast cancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jimaging9030065","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-574727","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10058454","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85152408233","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36976116","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-05531dc6-2e12-4251-94d7-ef278f77af3b"],"keyword":["FDG-PET/CT","Q.Clear","metastatic breast cancer","reconstruction algorithm"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-52F475A3DB57C254C418D60CC7AFDE76"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/224960912/jimaging_09_00065.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/jimaging9030065","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department at Clinical Engineering, Region of Southern Denmark, 6200 Aabenraa, Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ge healthcare","name":"GE Healthcare","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad","key":"naghavibehzadpau","last":"Naghavi-Behzad","locid":"223eadef-1216-4340-9b77-b3010eeba22f","name":"Naghavi-Behzad, Mohammad","orcid":"0000-0002-6761-8126","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"vogsenpau","last":"Vogsen","locid":"a69bc83c-c4ec-4214-a202-7c888490d1ca","name":"Vogsen, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0002-6124-4063","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oke","key":"gerkepau","last":"Gerke","locid":"596baeb1-6754-4d53-948f-30470dd1d976","name":"Gerke, Oke","orcid":"0000-0001-6335-3303","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Elisabeth","key":"dahlsgaardwalleniuspau","last":"Dahlsgaard-Wallenius","locid":"09dbda03-897a-47e9-8ce4-7c2e523c417c","name":"Dahlsgaard-Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette Juel","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","name":"Nissen, Henriette Juel","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nick Møldrup","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"139cc212-c0bb-4dd5-9a9e-9b6478b3b79c","name":"Jakobsen, Nick Møldrup","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul-Erik","key":"braadpau","last":"Braad","locid":"7df4b5a6-a971-420c-b424-ccc861b7f5ff","name":"Braad, Poul-Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-4906-5422","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mie Holm","key":"vilstruppau","last":"Vilstrup","locid":"9ceb6215-deb0-460f-8c59-bbc32b7dca27","name":"Vilstrup, Mie Holm","orcid":"0000-0002-4760-0068","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"deakpau","last":"Deak","name":"Deak, Paul","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Grubbe","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"89ec551d-ddfe-45e8-983a-f2bbc54f8a0e","name":"Hildebrandt, Malene Grubbe","orcid":"0000-0003-2720-9018","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Lund","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8a904314-798c-4e45-9559-b997a4e1d5c7","name":"Andersen, Thomas Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-2860-6317","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36976116"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/jimaging9030065","issn":["2313433X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Imaging","paperid":"65","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Journal of Imaging","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85152408233"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-05531dc6-2e12-4251-94d7-ef278f77af3b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comparison of Image Quality and Quantification Parameters between Q.Clear and OSEM Reconstruction Methods on FDG-PET/CT Images in Patients with Metastatic Breast Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-574727","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We present a transformation of the Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graph constraint based process specification language to safe Petri Nets with inhibitor and read arcs, generalized with an acceptance criteria enabling the specification of the union of regular and ω -regular languages. We prove that the DCR graph and the resulting Petri Net are bisimilar and that the bisimulation respects the acceptance criterium. The transformation enables the capturing of regular and omega-regular process requirements from texts and event logs using existing tools for DCR requirements mapping and process mining. A representation of DCR Graphs as Petri Nets advances the understanding of the relationship between the two models and enables improved analysis and model checking capabilities for DCR graph specifications through mature Petri net tools. We provide a python script implementing the transformation from the DCR XML export format to the PNML exchange format extended with arc types. In the implementation, all read arcs are replaced by a pair of standard input and output arcs. This directly enables the simulation and analysis of the resulting Petri Nets in tools such as TAPAAL, but means that the acceptance criterium for infinite runs is not preserved.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cosma, Vlad Paul","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739993"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-30","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2023-06-25","title":"44th International Conference on Application and Theory of Petri Nets and Concurrency, PETRI NETS 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bisimilarity","DCR Graphs","Petri nets"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transforming dynamic condition response graphs to safe petri nets","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/410854117/Transforming_Dynamic_Condition_Response.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-739993","identifier":[{"id":"85173572491","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e68db2bf-9706-456c-9847-c0c4bdfe9752"],"keyword":["Bisimilarity","DCR graphs","Petri Nets"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BFD029C5368CEA53067C5FA588A72C55"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/410854117/Transforming_Dynamic_Condition_Response.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["KMD A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Vlad Paul","key":"cosmapau","last":"Cosma","locid":"2e80a2e2-1e2e-49ee-933c-fe4a76cc2586","name":"Cosma, Vlad Paul","orcid":"0000-0001-8022-6402","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Luis","key":"gomespedh","last":"Gomes","name":"Gomes, Luis","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Robert","key":"lorenzpedh","last":"Lorenz","name":"Lorenz, Robert","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-33620-1_22","isbn":["9783031336195"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"417-439","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Application and Theory of Petri Nets and Concurrency - 44th International Conference, PETRI NETS 2023, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173572491"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","kmd a/s (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e68db2bf-9706-456c-9847-c0c4bdfe9752"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transforming Dynamic Condition Response Graphs to Safe Petri Nets","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739993","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Choreographic models express coordination between business roles, in contrast to standard process models that merge local control flow and communication between parties. A choreography is realizable, also known as endpoint projectable, if the independent behaviour of each role in composition with other roles, only behaves exactly in the same way as described in the choreography. We introduce a novel choreographic language expressing safety and liveness properties, incorporating multi-perspective constraints in communication flows, data, and time. This language builds upon recent developments in declarative choreographies using the Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graph formalism and extends it to accommodate data and time. The interaction between multiple dimensions can render models unrealizable, so we determine the conditions required for realizability through causal relationships within multi-perspective declarative choreographies. This way, realizable choreographies are guaranteed freedom of conflicts in the message exchanges that otherwise can lead to deadlocks.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","López, Hugo A.","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739015"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-15","place":"Utrecht, nl","start":"2023-09-11","title":"Proceedings of the 21st International Conference on Business Process Management, BPM 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Choreographies","Declarative models","Multi Perspective Process Modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"declarative choreographies with time and data","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/410854049/Declarative_Choreographies_with_Time_and_Data.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-739015","identifier":[{"id":"85172671850","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-445f1d66-c8c5-458a-b6f8-5dadd6a136fc"],"keyword":["Choreographies","Declarative Models","Multi-Perspective Process Modelling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-E06AA4BDA000A38ADF58D38144377247"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/410854049/Declarative_Choreographies_with_Time_and_Data.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hugo A.","key":"lópezpau","last":"López","name":"López, Hugo A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Chiara","key":"difrancescomarinopedh","last":"Di Francescomarino","name":"Di Francescomarino, Chiara","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrea","key":"burattinpedh","last":"Burattin","name":"Burattin, Andrea","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"janieschpedh","last":"Janiesch","name":"Janiesch, Christian","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Shazia","key":"sadiqpedh","last":"Sadiq","name":"Sadiq, Shazia","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-41623-1_5","isbn":["9783031416224"],"issn":["18651348"],"pages":"73-89","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Business Information Processing","status":"p","title":"Business Process Management Forum - BPM 2023 Forum, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85172671850"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-445f1d66-c8c5-458a-b6f8-5dadd6a136fc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Declarative Choreographies with Time and Data","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739015","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Smart contracts executed on blockchains are interactive programs where external actors generate events that trigger function invocations. Events can be emitted by participants asynchronously. However, some functionalities should be restricted to participants inhabiting specific roles in the system, which might be dynamically adjusted while the system evolves. We argue that current smart contract languages adopting imperative programming paradigms require additional complicated access control code. Furthermore, smart contracts are often developed independently and cannot share a joint access control policy. We propose to use Dynamic Condition Response Graphs for role-based and declarative access control for smart contracts. We show that they allow to capture and visualize a form of dynamic access control where access rights evolve as the contract state progresses. Their use supports straight-forward declaration of access control rights, improved code auditing, programming error reduction and improves users’ understanding of smart contracts","author_count":4,"contributors":["Xu, Yibin","Slaats, Tijs","Düdder, Boris","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-678493"],"event":{"end":"2023-05-15","place":"Melbourne, au","start":"2023-05-14","title":"2023 IEEE/ACM International Conference on Software and System Processes (ICSSP)","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adding generic role and process based behaviors to smart contracts using dynamic condition response graphs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/410853993/Adding_Generic.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-678493","identifier":[{"id":"85166173364","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7bcf8b1b-c505-4917-9bc7-d6774989ccd3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-18826BB533B046BDA24EC3E401990EE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/410853993/Adding_Generic.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yibin","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","locid":"08a435ed-3aab-4eec-88f1-c4e8c74b7155","name":"Xu, Yibin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Boris","key":"düdderpau","last":"Düdder","locid":"26641b70-8c76-4150-ae85-086cfa904763","name":"Düdder, Boris","orcid":"0000-0002-0241-7729","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Troels","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas Troels","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icssp59042.2023.00017","eisbn":["9798350311969"],"isbn":["9798350311976"],"pages":"70-80","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2023 IEEE/ACM International Conference on Software and System Processes (ICSSP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85166173364"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7bcf8b1b-c505-4917-9bc7-d6774989ccd3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Adding Generic Role- and Process-based Behaviors to Smart Contracts using Dynamic Condition Response Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-678493","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To assess long-term outcomes of restrictive versus standard intravenous (IV) fluid therapy in adult intensive care unit (ICU) patients with septic shock included in the European Conservative versus Liberal Approach to Fluid Therapy in Septic Shock in Intensive Care (CLASSIC) trial. Methods: We conducted the pre-planned analyses of mortality, health-related quality of life (HRQoL) using EuroQol (EQ)-5D-5L index values and EQ visual analogue scale (VAS), and cognitive function using Mini Montreal Cognitive Assessment (Mini MoCA) test at 1 year. Deceased patients were assigned numerical zero for HRQoL as a state equal to death and zero for cognitive function outcomes as worst possible score, and we used multiple imputation for missing data on HRQoL and cognitive function. Results: Among 1554 randomized patients, we obtained 1-year data on mortality in 97.9% of patients, HRQoL in 91.3%, and cognitive function in 86.3%. One-year mortality was 385/746 (51.3%) in the restrictive-fluid group versus 383/767 (49.9%) in the standard-fluid group, absolute risk difference 1.5%-points [99% confidence interval (CI) − 4.8 to 7.8]. Mean differences were 0.00 (99% CI − 0.06 to 0.05) for EQ-5D-5L index values, − 0.65 for EQ VAS (− 5.40 to 4.08), and − 0.14 for Mini MoCA (− 1.59 to 1.14) for the restrictive-fluid group versus the standard-fluid group. The results for survivors only were similar in both groups. Conclusions: Among adult ICU patients with septic shock, restrictive versus standard IV fluid therapy resulted in similar survival, HRQoL, and cognitive function at 1 year, but clinically important differences could not be ruled out.","author_count":63,"contributors":["Kjær, Maj Brit Nørregaard","Meyhoff, Tine Sylvest","Sivapalan, Praleene","Granholm, Anders","Hjortrup, Peter Buhl","Madsen, Martin Bruun","Møller, Morten Hylander","Egerod, Ingrid","Wetterslev, Jørn","Lange, Theis","Cronhjort, Maria","Laake, Jon Henrik","Jakob, Stephan M.","Nalos, Marek","Oste