ohort study (PLOT-ICU)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-091.33-715671","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Choreographic models express coordination between business roles, in contrast to standard process models that merge local control flow and communication between parties. A choreography is realizable, also known as endpoint projectable, if the independent behaviour of each role in composition with other roles, only behaves exactly in the same way as described in the choreography. We introduce a novel choreographic language expressing safety and liveness properties, incorporating multi perspective constraints in communication flows, data, and time. This language builds upon recent developments in declarative choreographies using the Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graph formalism and extends it to accommodate data and time. The interaction between multiple dimensions can render models unrealizable, so we determine the conditions required for realizability through causal relationships within multi-perspective declarative choreographies. This way, realizable choreographies are guaranteed freedom of conflicts in the message exchanges that otherwise can lead to deadlocks.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","López-Acosta, Hugo-Andrés","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689080"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-15","place":"Utrecht, nl","start":"2023-09-11","title":"21st International Conference of Business Process Management","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Choreographies","Declarative models","Multi Perspective Process Modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"declarative choreographies with time and data","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/333415706/BPM23_Forum_Declarative_Choreographies_with_Time_and_Data_5_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-689080","identifier":[{"id":"85172671850","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d34bc186-4da7-40ae-8711-0bf09b654fab"],"keyword":["Choreographies","Declarative Models","Multi-Perspective Process Modelling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-E06AA4BDA000A38ADF58D38144377247"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/333415706/BPM23_Forum_Declarative_Choreographies_with_Time_and_Data_5_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Software Systems Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hugo-Andrés","key":"lópezacostapau","last":"López-Acosta","locid":"c6f24f03-a51a-41aa-8767-60bae4767879","name":"López-Acosta, Hugo-Andrés","orcid":"0000-0001-5162-7936","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-41623-1_5","pages":"73-89","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the the 21st International Conference of Business Process Management","volume":"490"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85172671850"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d34bc186-4da7-40ae-8711-0bf09b654fab"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Declarative Choreographies with Time and Data","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-689080","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We present DCRSec, a confidentially aware declarative process language with data that employs data-dependent security levels and an information flow monitor that prevents the violation of information flow policies. Data-dependent security levels have been used to shape precise information flow policies and properly identify security compartments. We use an illustrative example to show that it also models process instances in a flexible but precise way. The semantics of the language is based on a version of the Dynamic Condition Response Graph language, which allows for declaring data-aware, event-based processes with finitary and infinitary computations subject to liveness properties and dynamically spawned sub-processes. The key technical contribution is to provide a termination-insensitive information flow monitor and prove non-interference, a soundness property, and transparency in all traces of DCRSec processes.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Geraldo, Eduardo","Seco, João Costa","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739741"],"event":{"end":"2023-10-23","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2023-10-22","title":"25th International Symposium on Principles and Practice of Declarative Programming, PPDP 2023 - As part of the ACM SIGPLAN conference on Systems, Programming, Languages, and Applications: Software for Humanity, SPLASH 2023, including LOPSTR 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NOVA University Lisbon"],"keyword":["Business processes","DCR Graphs","Information flow control","Privacy","Security Monitoring","Software Security"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data dependent confidentiality in dcr graphs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3610612.3610619","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-739741","identifier":[{"id":"85175452733","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bc545749-4142-4c20-8adc-3f4562b3f53b"],"keyword":["Business Processes","DCR Graphs","Information Flow Control","Privacy","Security Monitoring","Software Security"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CFBE8F5F2CB5FB54E5CA035C5A2C543B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/390399155/3610612.3610619.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3610612.3610619","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"nova university lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"NOVA University Lisbon","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Eduardo","key":"geraldopau","last":"Geraldo","name":"Geraldo, Eduardo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"João Costa","key":"secopau","last":"Seco","name":"Seco, João Costa","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3610612.3610619","eisbn":["9798400708121"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 25th International Symposium on Principles and Practice of Declarative Programming (PPDP 2023)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175452733"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bc545749-4142-4c20-8adc-3f4562b3f53b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Data-Dependent Confidentiality in DCR Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739741","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We present a method and prototype tool supporting participatory mapping of domain activities to event data recorded in information systems via the system interfaces. The aim is to facilitate responsible secondary use of event data recorded in information systems, such as process mining and the construction of predictive AI models. Another identified possible benefit is the support for increasing the quality of data by using the mapping to support educating new users in how to register data, thereby increasing the consistency in how domain activities are recorded. We illustrate the method on two cases, one from a job center in a danish municipality and another from a danish hospital using the healthcare platform from Epic.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Cosma, Vlad Paul","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Gyldenkærne, Christopher H.","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S02-094.28-704587"],"event":{"end":"2022-10-28","place":"Bozen-Bolzano, it","start":"2022-10-23","title":"International Workshops on EDBA, ML4PM, RPM, PODS4H, SA4PM, PQMI, EduPM, and DQT-PM, held at the International Conference on Process Mining, ICPM 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Data quality","Event extraction","Event matching","Participatory Design","Secondary use"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bermuda participatory mapping of domain activities to event data via system interfaces","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-27815-0_10","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-094.28-704587","identifier":[{"id":"85152584709","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c1d910a2-fa57-44f8-8e41-19a7ac42072d","ruc-c3764d9b-7867-40a7-b338-a8967b805c1b"],"keyword":["Data quality","Event extraction","Event matching","Participatory design","Secondary use"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-970F4110E5FCBF4C9D06BDA0FD804153"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/372960953/978_3_031_27815_0_138_150.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-27815-0_10","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/92988960/978_3_031_27815_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["KMD A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Programming, Logic and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":