,"locid":"d6406dea-1bcb-447c-88ae-926841ba574d","name":"Espelund, Ulrick","name_org":"Espelund, Ulrick Skipper","orcid":"0000-0002-3659-650X","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vibeke","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Vibeke","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolai","key":"haasepau","last":"Haase","name":"Haase, Nicolai","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"pernerpau","last":"Perner","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36263897"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14157","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"76-85","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141525308"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-54fc80e4-96a1-4df7-bea8-ab067d6bd25a","au-24eeb516-8696-420f-9b42-766e9f782a2e","sdu-d7d06e58-1d0d-4640-b65a-c2432952f697"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Thromboembolic and bleeding events in ICU patients with COVID-19 : A nationwide, observational study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-091.33-004156","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To assess the incidence, risk factors, and outcomes of atrial fibrillation (AF) in the ICU and to describe current practice in the management of AF. DESIGN: Multicenter, prospective, inception cohort study. SETTING: Forty-four ICUs in 12 countries in four geographical regions. SUBJECTS: Adult, acutely admitted ICU patients without a history of persistent/permanent AF or recent cardiac surgery were enrolled; inception periods were from October 2020 to June 2021. INTERVENTIONS: None. MEASUREMENTS AND MAIN RESULTS: We included 1,423 ICU patients and analyzed 1,415 (99.4%), among whom 221 patients had 539 episodes of AF. Most (59%) episodes were diagnosed with continuous electrocardiogram monitoring. The incidence of AF was 15.6% (95% CI, 13.8-17.6), of which newly developed AF was 13.3% (11.5-15.1). A history of arterial hypertension, paroxysmal AF, sepsis, or high disease severity at ICU admission was associated with AF. Used interventions to manage AF were fluid bolus 19% (95% CI 16-23), magnesium 16% (13-20), potassium 15% (12-19), amiodarone 51% (47-55), beta-1 selective blockers 34% (30-38), calcium channel blockers 4% (2-6), digoxin 16% (12-19), and direct current cardioversion in 4% (2-6). Patients with AF had more ischemic, thromboembolic (13.6% vs 7.9%), and severe bleeding events (5.9% vs 2.1%), and higher mortality (41.2% vs 25.2%) than those without AF. The adjusted cause-specific hazard ratio for 90-day mortality by AF was 1.38 (95% CI, 0.95-1.99). CONCLUSIONS: In ICU patients, AF occurred in one of six and was associated with different conditions. AF was associated with worse outcomes while not statistically significantly associated with 90-day mortality in the adjusted analyses. We observed variations in the diagnostic and management strategies for AF.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Wetterslev, Mik","Møller, Morten Hylander","Granholm, Anders","Hassager, Christian","Haase, Nicolai","Lange, Theis","Myatra, Sheila N.","Hästbacka, Johanna","Arabi, Yaseen M.","Shen, Jiawei","Cronhjort, Maria","Lindqvist, Elin","Aneman, Anders","Young, Paul J.","Szczeklik, Wojciech","Siegemund, Martin","Koster, Thijs","Aslam, Tayyba Naz","Bestle, Morten H.","Girkov, Mia S.","Kalvit, Kushal","Mohanty, Rakesh","Mascarenhas, Joanne","Pattnaik, Manoranjan","Vergis, Sara","Haranath, Sai Praveen","Shah, Mehul","Joshi, Ziyokov","Wilkman, Erika","Reinikainen, Matti","Lehto, Pasi","Jalkanen, Ville","Pulkkinen, Anni","An, Youzhong","Wang, Guoxing","Huang, Lei","Huang, Bin","Liu, Wei","Gao, Hengbo","Dou, Lin","Li, Shuangling","Yang, Wanchun","Tegnell, Emily","Perner, Anders","Poulsen, Lone M.","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Andreasen, Anne Sofie","Kristiansen, Klaus Tjelle","Mohr, Thomas","Møller, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689780"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["the AFIB-ICU collaborators"],"country":["Australia","China","Finland","India","Netherlands","New Zealand","Norway","Poland","Saudi Arabia","Sweden","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Apollo Hospitals","Breach Candy Hospital","Capital & Coast District Health Board","Capital Medical University","Hebei Medical University","Jagiellonian University Medical College","Jyvaskyla Central Hospital","Karolinska Institutet","Liverpool Hospital","MOSC Medical College","Medical Research Institute of New Zealand","Ministry of National Guard – Health Affairs","Peking University","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Scb Medical College and Hospital","Sir H. N. Reliance Foundation Hospital and Research Centre","Tagore Hospital P. Ltd.","Tampere University Hospital","Tata Memorial Hospital","Tianjin First Central Hospital","University of Basel","University of Eastern Finland","University of Groningen","University of Helsinki","University of New South Wales","University