111/aas.14007","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"375-385","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121116321"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-44bb0278-8df0-415b-ab44-686b12cf0bd2","sdu-e67a8dce-abad-4383-8a50-26e54f6233b2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Management of acute atrial fibrillation in the intensive care unit : An international survey","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-741355","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Histamine (HA) is an indicator of food freshness and quality. However, high concentrations of HA can cause food poisoning. Simple, rapid, sensitive, and specific quantification can enable efficient screening of HA in food and beverages. However, conventional assays are complicated and time-consuming, as they require multiple incubation, washing, and separation steps. Here, we demonstrate that time-gated Förster resonance energy transfer (TG-FRET) between terbium (Tb) complexes and organic dyes can be implemented in both immunosensors and aptasensors for simple HA quantification using a rapid, single-step, mix-and-measure assay format. Both biosensors could quantify HA at concentrations relevant in food poisoning with limits of detection of 0.19 μg/mL and 0.03 μg/mL, respectively. Excellent specificity was documented against the structurally similar food components tryptamine and l-histidine. Direct applicability of the TG-FRET assays was demonstrated by quantifying HA in spiked fish and wine samples with both excellent concentration recovery and agreement with conventional multistep enzyme-linked immunosorbent assays (ELISAs). Our results show that the simplicity and rapidity of TG-FRET assays do not compromise sensitivity, specificity, and reliability, and both immunosensors and aptasensors have a strong potential for their implementation in advanced food safety screening.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fu, Hui Jun","Su, Ruifang","Luo, Lin","Chen, Zi Jian","Sørensen, Thomas Just","Hildebrandt, Niko","Xu, Zhen Lin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-447549"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","France","South Korea"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","FHU CARNAVAL","Paris-Saclay University","Seoul National University","South China Agricultural University"],"keyword":["Aptasensors","Fluorescence","Förster resonance energy transfer","Immunoassays"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rapid and wash free time gated fret histamine assays using antibodies and aptamers","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/357520815/Revised_Manuscript.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-447549","identifier":[{"id":"35312279","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85127868209","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5a74316f-f8c1-4b77-a6d7-bd0fb9088096"],"keyword":["Förster resonance energy transfer","aptasensors","fluorescence","food testing","immunoassays"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D6EF524ADA5C946D52B2CA4CDE19E352"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/357520815/Revised_Manuscript.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"fhu carnaval","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"FHU CARNAVAL","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"south china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"kr","key":"seoul national university","loc":["South Korea","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Seoul National University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fr","key":"paris saclay university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Paris-Saclay University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Hui Jun","key":"fupau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Hui Jun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ruifang","key":"supau","last":"Su","locid":"c9b48be8-ba59-454b-ad5b-251aeac6ff74","name":"Su, Ruifang","orcid":"0000-0003-3328-0136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lin","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Lin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Zi Jian","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Zi Jian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thomas Just","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"0744dbfc-1b71-4ed8-8fee-84ddc6005b6b","name":"Sørensen, Thomas Just","orcid":"0000-0003-1491-5116","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 5","first":"Niko","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Niko","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Zhen Lin","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Zhen Lin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35312279"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acssensors.2c00085","issn":["23793694"],"issue":"4","journal":"ACS Sensors","pages":"1113-1121","status":"p","title":"ACS Sensors","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127868209"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5a74316f-f8c1-4b77-a6d7-bd0fb9088096"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Rapid and Wash-Free Time-Gated FRET Histamine Assays Using Antibodies and Aptamers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-447549","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Artificial intelligence (AI) is seen as a major disrupting force in the future healthcare system. However, the assessment of the value of AI technologies is still unclear. Therefore, a multidisciplinary group of experts and patients developed a Model for ASsessing the value of AI (MAS-AI) in medical imaging. Medical imaging is chosen due to the maturity of AI in this area, ensuring a robust evidence-based model. METHODS: MAS-AI was developed in three phases. First, a literature review of existing guides, evaluations, and assessments of the value of AI in the field of medical imaging. Next, we interviewed leading researchers in AI in Denmark. The third phase consisted of two workshops where decision makers, patient organizations, and researchers discussed crucial topics for evaluating AI. The multidisciplinary team revised the model between workshops according to comments. RESULTS: The MAS-AI guideline consists of two steps covering nine domains and five process factors supporting the assessment. Step 1 contains a description of patients, how the AI model was developed, and initial ethical and legal considerations. In step 2, a multidisciplinary assessment of outcomes of the AI application is done for the five remaining domains: safety, clinical aspects, economics, organizational aspects, and patient aspects. CONCLUSIONS: We have developed an health technology assessment-based framework to support the introduction of AI technologies into healthcare in medical imaging. It is essential to ensure informed and valid decisions regarding the adoption of AI with a structured process and tool. MAS-AI can help support decision making and provide greater transparency for all parties.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Fasterholdt, Iben","Kjølhede, Tue","Naghavi-Behzad, Mohammad","Schmidt, Thomas","Rautalammi, Quinnie T S","Hildebrandt, Malene Grubbe","Gerdes, Anne","Barkler, Astrid","Kidholm, Kristian","Rac, Valeria E","Rasmussen, Benjamin Schnack"],"