st":"Norman","name":"Norman, Håkon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Artem","key":"polyvyanyypedh","last":"Polyvyanyy","name":"Polyvyanyy, Artem","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Moe Thandar","key":"wynnpedh","last":"Wynn","name":"Wynn, Moe Thandar","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Amy Van","key":"looypedh","last":"Looy","name":"Looy, Amy Van","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manfred","key":"reichertpedh","last":"Reichert","name":"Reichert, Manfred","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"161-178","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","title":"Business process management - 19th international conference, BPM 2021, rome, italy, september 06-10, 2021, proceedings","volume":"12875"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0dbcb580-ca0b-451a-96f9-9a374201ab1d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Zoom and enhance: Action refinement via subprocesses in timed declarative processes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381470","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"When designing artificial intelligence (AI) in politicised contexts, such as the public sector, optimistic promises of what AI can achieve often shape decisions around which problems AI should address. Different epistemological views carry different understandings of what is considered the problem at hand, and, as we show in this paper, ethnographic perspectives often fail to match the politicised promises of AI. This paper reflects on personal experiences from an interdisciplinary research project that aimed to take a responsible approach to research and design AI for public services in Denmark. Seeking alternatives to the inflexible algorithms [3, 38] often used to automate or augment specific decision-making tasks in these contexts [1, 2, 35], our research project took a flexible approach to research and design and included ethnographic workplace studies to explore whether AI could both leverage the increasing powers of computing and retain the discretion of the user [23]. Following Mesman [33], we present three empirical moments that were particularly challenging for us as ethnographic researchers and influenced our project in important ways regarding the problems for AI to solve. Problematising [6] them, enabled us to surface how 'readiness', emerging from the politicised context of AI in Denmark, had confounded our efforts at interdisciplinary collaboration. Problematisation, then, allowed us to come to a new understanding of the problem at hand and open up a space to collaboratively re-imagine the problems for AI to solve. This paper is in the spirit of serving as a bridge between our initial and revised understanding, pointing to the ongoing discussion in HCI about 'bridging the gap' between ethnography and design. Our contribution is a discussion of how researchers and designers might engage with problematisation at the frontiers of HCI to develop an open-ended approach to collaborative AI design in politicised contexts.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Petersen, Anette C.M.","Cohn, Marisa Leavitt","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Møller, Naja Holten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-485905"],"event":{"end":"2021-07-13","place":"Virtual, Online, it","start":"2021-07-11","title":"14th Biannual Conference of the Italian SIGCHI Chapter: Frontiers of HCI, CHItaly 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ethnography","Interdisciplinary research","Politics","Problematisation","Public services"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thinking problematically as a resource for ai design in politicised contexts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/281989572/_Thinking_Problematically_as_a_Resource_for_AI_Design_in.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-485905","identifier":[{"id":"85112707591","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9ab0e7e6-ffe8-4b3d-a7f2-4e96491c4429"],"keyword":["AI design","Ethnography","Interdisciplinary research","Politics","Problematisation","Public digitisation","Public services"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F71E748B4749B92B824AE625C62584C4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/281989572/_Thinking_Problematically_as_a_Resource_for_AI_Design_in.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Anette C.M.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Anette C.M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marisa Leavitt","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","name":"Cohn, Marisa Leavitt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Naja Holten","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"1373f0c3-8420-4023-874a-25270bf667d6","name":"Møller, Naja Holten","orcid":"0000-0002-4324-3745","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3464385.3464738","eisbn":["9781450389778"],"pages":"1-8","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM International Conference Proceeding Series","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 14th Biannual Conference of the Italian SIGCHI Chapter","title":"CHItaly 2021 - Frontiers of HCI"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85112707591"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9ab0e7e6-ffe8-4b3d-a7f2-4e96491c4429"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"'Thinking problematically' as a resource for AI design in politicised contexts","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-485905","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background Thrombocytopenia is frequent in intensive care unit (ICU) patients and may be associated with adverse outcomes. We aimed to assess the incidence, risk factors, and outcomes associated with thrombocytopenia in adult ICU patients. Methods We conducted a scoping review in accordance with the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Review and Meta-analyses extension for Scoping Reviews (PRISMA-ScR) and the Grading of Recommendations, Assessment, Development and Evaluation (GRADE) approach. We included study reports on adult ICU patients with thrombocytopenia and assessed patient-important outcomes, including mortality and health-related quality-of-life. Results We included a total of 70 studies comprising a total of 215 098 patients; 57 were cohort studies. The incidence of thrombocytopenia varied from 8 to 56 per 100 admissions (very low quality of evidence). We identified several risk factors including age, sepsis, and higher disease severity (low quality of evidence). Thrombocytopenia was associated with bleeding, use of life support, length of stay in the ICU, and increased mortality (low/very low quality of evidence). Data on platelet transfusion before invasive procedures and transfusion thresholds were limited. No studies assessed the benefits and harms of thromboprophylaxis in ICU patients with thrombocytopenia. Conclusions Thrombocytopenia is common and associated with increased morbidity and mortality in adult ICU patients. Several risk factors for thrombocytopenia exists, but the evidence-base on management strategies, including transfusion thresholds and thromboprophylaxis in ICU patients is very limited.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jonsson, Andreas Bender","Rygård, Sofie Louise","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Perner, Anders","Møller, Morten Hylander","Russell, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-499608"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thrombocytopenia in intensive care unit patients a scoping review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-499608","identifier":[{"id":"85091487603","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32916017","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b1c9fa86-a69c-4511-ab00-c46c04d3ee13"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9FA6B0E62897CAAAFEE7AD432B6CC27B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen Academy for Medical Education and Simulation"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Andreas Bender","key":"jonssonpau","last":"Jonsson","name":"Jonsson, Andreas Bender","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sofie Louise","key":"rygårdpau","last":"Rygård","name":"Rygård, Sofie Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"pernerpau","last":"Perner","locid":"8a389541-d529-4ee3-8364-66bfc85f77c9","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Hylander","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"9463b017-3c43-470d-b95b-cf3cba8a27d4","name":"Møller, Morten Hylander","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene","key":"russellpau","last":"Russell","name":"Russell, Lene","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32916017"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.13699","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"2-14","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"65"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091487603"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b1c9fa86-a69c-4511-ab00-c46c04d3ee13"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Thrombocytopenia in intensive care unit patients : A scoping review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-499608","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper addresses the open technical problems of evolving executable, event-based process models by refinement, that is, by iteratively expanding a model until it has the required level of detail. Such iterative development is helpful because of the expectation that the next-step model is semantically compatible with the previous one, only with more detail. We provide in this paper a formal notion of refinement of single atomic actions (events) into entire subprocesses, and a theoretical framework for providing guarantees that such a next-step model is formally a refinement of the previous one. Our work is set within the declarative, event-based process modelling language of timed Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graphs, which can express timed constraints (conditions with delay and obligations with deadlines) between events, liveness, safety, and concurrency. Concretely, we extend DCR graph syntax and semantics with a notion of subprocess, provide examples of its use, and give sound approximations of situations where replacing an event with a subprocess formally is a refinement of the original process.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Normann, Håkon","Debois, Søren","Slaats, Tijs","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-529118"],"event":{"acronym":"BPM","end":"2021-09-10","place":"Rome, it","start":"2021-09-06","title":"19th International Conference on Business Process Management, BPM 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Action refinement","DCR Graphs","Decomposition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"zoom and enhance action refinement via subprocesses in timed declarative processes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-529118","identifier":[{"id":"85115199701","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e334f24b-668f-478d-9c20-53a84b03e9bd"],"keyword":["Action refinement","DCR graphs","Decomposition","Subprocesses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-60A646DD3C83DBD4806F89316EE85542"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["DCR Solutions A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Håkon","key":"normannpau","last":"Normann","locid":"68370c00-7aca-4a84-97cd-509727ec4a96","name":"Normann, Håkon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-00