Kolstrup","name":"Kolstrup, Line","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mariusz","key":"boczanmariuszpau","last":"Boczan","name":"Boczan, Mariusz","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bodil S.","key":"rasmussenbodilspau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Bodil S.","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Iben S.","key":"darfeltibenspau","last":"Darfelt","name":"Darfelt, Iben S.","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ville","key":"jalkanenvillepau","last":"Jalkanen","name":"Jalkanen, Ville","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pasi","key":"lehtopasipau","last":"Lehto","name":"Lehto, Pasi","rank":47,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matti","key":"reinikainenmattipau","last":"Reinikainen","name":"Reinikainen, Matti","rank":48,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sigurbergur","key":"kárasonsigurbergurpau","last":"Kárason","name":"Kárason, Sigurbergur","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristinn","key":"sigvaldasonkristinnpau","last":"Sigvaldason","name":"Sigvaldason, Kristinn","rank":50,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34870855"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14007","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"375-385","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121116321"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c410a819-b705-478e-93f8-b0e0f87078a0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Management of acute atrial fibrillation in the intensive care unit : An international survey","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-510476","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Process design artifacts have been increasingly used to guide the modeling of business processes. To support users in designing and understanding process models, different process artifacts have been combined in several ways leading to the emergence of the so-called “hybrid process artifacts”. While many hybrid artifacts have been proposed in the literature, little is known about how they can actually support users in practice. To address this gap, this work investigates the way users engage with hybrid process artifacts during comprehension tasks. In particular, we focus on a hybrid representation of DCR Graphs (DCR-HR) combining a process model, textual annotations and an interactive simulation. Following a qualitative approach, we conduct a multi-granular analysis exploiting process mining, eye-tracking techniques, and verbal data analysis to scrutinize the reading patterns and the strategies adopted by users when being confronted with DCR-HR. The findings of the coarse-grained analysis provide important insights about the behavior of domain experts and IT specialists and show how user’s background and task type change the use of hybrid process artifacts. As for the fine-grained analysis, user’s behavior was classified into goal-directed and exploratory and different strategies of using the interactive simulation were identified. In addition, a progressive switch from an exploratory behavior to a goal-directed behavior was observed. These insights pave the way for an improved development of hybrid process artifacts and delineate several directions for future work.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Abbad Andaloussi, Amine","Zerbato, Francesca","Burattin, Andrea","Slaats, Tijs","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Weber, Barbara"],"cuid":["S02-096.23-034128"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Abbad Andaloussi, Amine"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of St. Gallen"],"keyword":["Behavioral analysis","DCR Graphs","Eye tracking","Hybrid process artifacts","Process models","Think aloud"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring how users engage with hybrid process artifacts based on declarative process models a behavioral analysis based on eye tracking and think aloud","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://rdcu.be/b5NuZ","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.23-034128","identifier":[{"id":"85087518307","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4418d42c-b650-4e3c-938b-177619688791","ku-a025357c-b919-475f-b3d4-ccc8d188e04a"],"keyword":["Behavioral analysis","DCR graphs","Eye-tracking","Hybrid process artifacts","Process models","Think-aloud"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0338A50B51576E8DE2AC6D0C742245EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/312635719/2020_sosym.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://rdcu.be/b5NuZ","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Software and Process Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"university of st gallen","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of St. Gallen","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amine","key":"abbadandaloussipau","last":"Abbad Andaloussi","locid":"ec567f0e-aa1c-42e2-a523-fccf2f03efbe","name":"Abbad Andaloussi, Amine","name_org":"Abbad Andaloussi, Amine","orcid":"0000-0002-3404-7849","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesca","key":"zerbatopau","last":"Zerbato","name":"Zerbato, Francesca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andrea","key":"burattinpau","last":"Burattin","locid":"75b43f3c-f477-4ac8-8717-c6d2b93bed02","name":"Burattin, Andrea","orcid":"0000-0002-0837-0183","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Barbara","key":"weberpau","last":"Weber","locid":"4bbfa31e-3aa1-4565-88b1-8c19946807e6","name":"Weber, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-6004-4860","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10270-020-00811-8","issn":["16191366","16191374"],"issn_org":["16191366"],"journal":"Software and Systems Modeling","pages":"1437-1464","status":"p","title":"Software and Systems Modeling","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087518307"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4418d42c-b650-4e3c-938b-177619688791","ku-a025357c-b919-475f-b3d4-ccc8d188e04a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring how users engage with hybrid process artifacts based on declarative process models : a behavioral analysis based on eye-tracking and think-aloud","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.23-034128","year":2021,"yearsub":2021}
{"abstract":"Background: In the early phase of the pandemic, some guidelines recommended the use of corticosteroids for critically ill patients with COVID-19, whereas others recommended against the use despite lack of firm evidence of either benefit or harm. In the COVID STEROID trial, we aimed to assess the effects of low-dose hydrocortisone on patient-centred outcomes in adults with COVID-19 and severe hypoxia. Methods: In this multicentre, parallel-group, placebo-controlled, blinded, centrally randomised, stratified clinical trial, we randomly assigned adults with confirmed COVID-19 and severe hypoxia (use of mechanical ventilation or supplementary oxygen with a flow of at least 10 L/min) to either hydrocortisone (200 mg/d) vs a matching placebo for 7 days or until hospital discharge. The primary outcome was the number of days alive without life support at day 28 after randomisation. Results: The trial was terminated early when 30 out of 1000 participants had been enrolled because of external evidence indicating benefit from corticosteroids in severe COVID-19. At day 28, the median number of days alive without life support in the hydrocortisone vs placebo group were 7 vs 10 (adjusted mean difference: −1.1 days, 95% CI −9.5 to 7.3, P =.79); mortality was 6/16 vs 2/14; and the number of serious adverse reactions 1/16 vs 0/14. Conclusions: In this trial of adults with COVID-19 and severe hypoxia, we were unable to provide precise estimates of the benefits and harms of hydrocortisone as compared with placebo as only 3% of the planned sample size were enrolled. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov: NCT04348305. European Union Drug Regulation Authorities Clinical Trials (EudraCT) Database: 2020-001395-15.","author_count":75,"contributors":["Munch, Marie Warrer","Meyhoff, Tine Sylvest","Helleberg, Marie","Kjær, Maj Brit Nørregaard","Granholm, Anders","Hjortsø, Carl Johan Steensen","Jensen, Thomas Steen","Møller, Morten Hylander","Hjortrup, Peter Buhl","Wetterslev, Mik","Vesterlund, Gitte Kingo","Russell, Lene","Jørgensen, Vibeke Lind","Kristiansen, Klaus Tjelle","Benfield, Thomas","Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","Andreasen, Anne Sofie","Bestle, Morten Heiberg","Poulsen, Lone Musaeus","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Knudsen, Lene Surland","Møller, Anders","Sølling, Christoffer Grant","Brøchner, Anne Craveiro","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Nielsen, Henrik","Christensen, Steffen","Strøm, Thomas","Cronhjort, Maria","Wahlin, Rebecka Rubenson","Jakob, Stephan M.","Cioccari, Luca","Venkatesh, Balasubramanian","Hammond, Naomi","Jha, Vivekanand","Myatra, Sheila Nainan","Jensen, Marie Qvist","Leistner, Jens Wolfgang","Mikkelsen, Vibe Sommer","Svenningsen, Jens S.","Laursen, Signe Bjørn","Hatley, Emma Victoria","Kristensen, Camilla Meno","Al-Alak, Ali","Clapp, Esben","Jonassen, Trine Bak","Bjerregaard, Caroline Løkke","Østerby, Niels Christian Haubjerg","Jespersen, Mette Mindedahl","Abou-Kassem, Dalia","Lassen, Mathilde Languille","Zaabalawi, Reem","Daoud, Mohammed Mahmoud","Abdi, Suhayb","Meier, Nick","la Cour, Kirstine","Derby, Cecilie Bauer","Damlund, Birka Ravnholt","Laigaard, Jens","Andersen, Lene Lund","Mikkelsen, Johan","Jensen, Jeppe Lundholm Stadarfeld","Rasmussen, Anders Hørby","Arnerlöv, Emil","Lykke, Mathilde","Holst-Hansen, Mikkel Zacharias Bystrup","Tøstesen, Boris Wied","Schwab, Janne","Madsen, Emilie Kabel","Gluud, Christian","Lange, Theis","Perner, Anders"],"cuid":["S04-096.30-009857"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Munch, Marie Warrer"],"country":["Australia","India","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Manipal Academy of Higher Education","Manipal University","Stockholm South General Hospital","Tata Memorial Hospital","University Hospital Bern","University Hospital of Bern","University of Bern","University of New South Wales"],"keyword":["Adult","Corticosteroids","Covid 19","Humans","Hydrocortisone","Hypoxia","Placebo controlled trial","Randomised clinical trial","SARS CoV 2","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low dose hydrocortisone in patients with covid 000000000019 and severe hypoxia the covid steroid randomised placebo controlled trial","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8441888/pdf/AAS-65-1421.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study is funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation, Grant/Award Number: 0062998 and supported by Rigshospitalet's Research Council, Grant/Award Number: E‐22703‐06 and Pfizer, Grant/Award Number: 60473019. The funding sources were not involved in designing, conducting, analysing or reporting of the COVID STEROID trial. The Department of Intensive Care, Rigshospitalet, has received funds for other research projects from the Novo Nordisk Foundation, Ferring and Fresenius Kabi. TB reports grants from Novo Nordisk Foundation, grants from Lundbeck Foundation, grants from Simonsen Foundation, grants and personal fees from GSK, grants and personal fees from Pfizer, personal fees from Boehringer Ingelheim, grants and personal fees from Gilead, personal fees from MSD, grants from Kai Hansen Foundation, outside the submitted work. CSU has received personal fees from AstraZeneca, GSK, Chiesi, TEVA, ALK‐Abello, Orion Pharma, Boehringer‐Ingelheim, Sanofi‐Genzyme, Novartis and Actelion outside the submitted work. The Department of Intensive Care Medicine, Bern University Hospital (Inselspital), has or has had research & development/consulting contracts with Edwards Lifesciences Services GmbH, Phagenesis Limited and Nestlé. The money was paid into a departmental fund, and none of the authors received any financial gain. The Department of Intensive Care Medicine, Bern University Hospital (Inselspital), has received unrestricted educational grants from the following organisations for organising bi‐annual postgraduate courses in the fields of critical care ultrasound, management of extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (ECMO) and mechanical ventilation: Pierre Fabre Pharma AG (formerly known as RobaPharm), Pfizer AG, Bard Medica SA, Abbott AG, Anandic Medical Systems, PanGas AG Healthcare, Orion Pharma, Bracco, Edwards Lifesciences AG, Hamilton Medical AG, Fresenius Kabi (Schweiz) AG, Getinge Group Maquet AG, Dräger Schweiz AG, and Teleflex Medical GmbH. The remaining authors have no conflicts of interest to declare."],"id":"S04-096.30-009857","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8441888","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85115113342","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34138478","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-cd616cd8-9974-4581-a13f-ee6af03ee1c7","au-d8268126-dc5b-46f9-affe-91abed2274a8","ku-15e1eeec-3995-48c7-854c-4f4e25f30962","sdu-04cd9874-8479-4592-ba28-08e108011723"],"keyword":["Adult","COVID-19","Humans","Hypoxia","SARS-CoV-2","Treatment Outcome","corticosteroids","hydrocortisone","placebo-controlled trial","randomised clinical trial"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-7B9A27C1123FEDF917F87049AD844263"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":