r Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of International Conference on Software and Systems Process"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092529434"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","dcr solutions a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cbaff1f9-829a-401c-88d1-79d34ba67628","ku-a11fcd9c-9dcc-4916-a4a7-2e012140fa90"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"EcoKnow: Engineering Effective, Co-created and Compliant Adaptive Case Management Systems for Knowledge Workers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.74-037184","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper examines the nature of discretion in social work in order to debunk myths dominating prevalent debates on digitisation and automation in the public sector. Social workers have traditionally used their discretion widely and with great autonomy, but discretion has increasingly come under pressure for its apparent subjectivity and randomness. In Denmark, our case in point, the government recently planned to standardise laws to limit or remove discretion where possible in order for automation of case management to gain a foothold. Recent studies have focused on discretion in the public sector, but few have examined it explicitly and as part of real cases. As a consequence, they often leave the myths about discretion unchallenged. Inspired by the literature on discretion and CSCW research on rules in action, this study reports on an empirical investigation of discretion in child protection services in Denmark. The results of our analysis provide a new understanding of discretion as a cooperative endeavour, based on consultation and skill, rather than an arbitrary or idiosyncratic choice. In this manner, our study contradicts the myth of discretion inherent in the automation agenda. Correspondingly, we ask for attention to be given to systems that integrate discretion with technology rather than seek to undermine it directly or get around it surreptitiously. In this age of automation, this is not only an important but also an urgent task for CSCW researchers to fulfil.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Petersen, Anette C.M.","Christensen, Lars Rune","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S02-094.12-038368"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Administrative work","Automation","Casework","Decision making","Digital ready legislation","Digitisation","Discretion","Rules in action","Social work"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of discretion in the age of automation","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85697258/AnetteC.M.Petersenetal.TheRoleofDiscretionintheAgeofAutomaion.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-094.12-038368","identifier":[{"id":"85078606508","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b7d5fa33-3fe8-44ba-ba7d-abbba6f1493e","ku-2322e320-f1f1-4fd9-8ad3-b1e370f7cfab"],"keyword":["Administrative work","Automation","Casework","Decision-making","Digital-ready legislation","Digitisation","Discretion","Rules in action","Social work"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AF2AF603BD6EAE2B77EAFF4DE9288442"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85697258/AnetteC.M.Petersenetal.TheRoleofDiscretionintheAgeofAutomaion.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Anette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10606-020-09371-3","issn":["09259724","15737551"],"issn_org":["09259724"],"issue":"3","journal":"Computer Supported Cooperative Work","pages":"303-333","status":"p","title":"Computer Supported Cooperative Work","title_org":"Computer Supported Cooperative Work: CSCW: An International Journal","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078606508"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b7d5fa33-3fe8-44ba-ba7d-abbba6f1493e","ku-2322e320-f1f1-4fd9-8ad3-b1e370f7cfab"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Role of Discretion in the Age of Automation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.12-038368","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus-2 has caused a pandemic of coronavirus disease (COVID-19) with many patients developing hypoxic respiratory failure. Corticosteroids reduce the time on mechanical ventilation, length of stay in the intensive care unit and potentially also mortality in similar patient populations. However, corticosteroids have undesirable effects, including longer time to viral clearance. Clinical equipoise on the use of corticosteroids for COVID-19 exists. Methods: The COVID STEROID trial is an international, randomised, stratified, blinded clinical trial. We will allocate 1000 adult patients with COVID-19 receiving ≥10 L/min of oxygen or on mechanical ventilation to intravenous hydrocortisone 200 mg daily vs placebo (0.9% saline) for 7 days. The primary outcome is days alive without life support (ie mechanical ventilation, circulatory support, and renal replacement therapy) at day 28. Secondary outcomes are serious adverse reactions at day 14; days alive without life support at day 90; days alive and out of hospital at day 90; all-cause mortality at day 28, day 90, and 1 year; and health-related quality of life at 1 year. We will conduct the statistical analyses according to this protocol, including interim analyses for every 250 patients followed for 28 days. The primary outcome will be compared using the Kryger Jensen and Lange test in the intention to treat population and reported as differences in means and medians with 95% confidence intervals. Discussion: The COVID STEROID trial will provide important evidence to guide the use of corticosteroids in COVID-19 and severe hypoxia.","author_count":49,"contributors":["Petersen, Marie Warrer","Meyhoff, Tine Sylvest","Helleberg, Marie","Kjær, Maj-Brit Nørregaard","Granholm, Anders","Hjortsø, Carl Johan Steensen","Jensen, Thomas Steen","Møller, Morten Hylander","Hjortrup, Peter Buhl","Wetterslev, Mik","Vesterlund, Gitte Kingo","Russell, Lene","Jørgensen, Vibeke Lind","Tjelle, Klaus","Benfield, Thomas","Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","Andreasen, Anne Sofie","Mohr, Thomas","Bestle, Morten H.","Poulsen, Lone Musaeus","Hitz, Mette Friberg","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Knudsen, Lene Surland","Møller, Anders","Sølling, Christoffer Grant","Brøchner, Anne Craveiro","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Nielsen, Henrik","Christensen, Steffen","Strøm, Thomas","Cronhjort, Maria","Wahlin, Rebecka Rubenson","Jakob, Stephan","Cioccari, Luca","Venkatesh, Balasubramanian","Hammond, Naomi","Jha, Vivekanand","Myatra, Sheila Nainan","Gluud, Christian","Lange, Theis","Perner, Anders"],"cuid":["S04-094.45-003929"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Petersen, Marie Warrer"],"country":["Australia","India","Sweden","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Manipal Academy of Higher Education","Manipal University","Tata Memorial Hospital","University Hospital of Bern","University of Bern","University of New South Wales"],"keyword":["Therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low dose hydrocortisone in patients with covid 000000000019 and severe hypoxia covid steroid trial protocol and statistical analysis plan","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7404666/pdf/AAS-9999-na.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors thank the clinical and research staff at all participating hospital departments, and all patients and relatives who have provided consent for participation in the trial, the funding sources, and the regulatory authorities for rapid case handling and approval. Balasubramanian Venkatesh have received financial support from the Medical Research Future Fund Australia. The Department of Intensive Care, Rigshospitalet, has received funds for other research projects from the Novo Nordisk Foundation, Ferring and Fresenius Kabi. Dr Benfield reports grants from Pfizer, grants from Novo Nordisk Foundation, grants from Lundbeck Foundation, grants from Simonsen Foundation, grants and personal fees from GSK, grants and personal fees from Pfizer, personal fees from Boehringer Ingelheim, grants and personal fees from Gilead, personal fees from MSD, grants from Lundbeck Foundation, grants from Kai Hansen Foundation, outside the submitted work. The Department of Intensive Care Medicine, Bern University Hospital (Inselspital), has or has had research & development/consulting contracts with Edwards Lifesciences Services GmbH, Phagenesis Limited and Nestlé. The money was paid into a departmental fund, and none of the authors received any financial gain. The Department of Intensive Care Medicine, Bern University Hospital (Inselspital), has received unrestricted educational grants from the following organisations for organising bi‐annual postgraduate courses in the fields of critical care ultrasound, management of extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (ECMO) and mechanical ventilation: Pierre Fabre Pharma AG (formerly known as RobaPharm), Pfizer AG, Bard Medica SA, Abbott AG, Anandic Medical Systems, PanGas AG Healthcare, Orion Pharma, Bracco, Edwards Lifesciences AG, Hamilton Medical AG, Fresenius Kabi (Schweiz) AG, Getinge Group Maquet AG, Dräger Schweiz AG, and Teleflex Medical GmbH. Dr Friberg Hitz has received grants from OrklaCare, UCB, Ellab Fond and Amgen, and received personal payment in relation to lectures and advisory boards, none of which have any relation to the present trial. The remaining authors have no conflicts of interests to declare."],"id":"S04-094.45-003929","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7404666","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85088805682","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32779728","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000553795500001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-506735a6-0d41-4e1c-9839-b2aa4c38085c","au-dff80599-eb40-4a79-a376-7558114ac69d","ku-f90ea239-809a-41e7-bbcb-b7cb217224f1","sdu-b9a84bc8-4dc8-4629-b0e0-e82e3acd1571"],"keyword":["THERAPY"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-51EEDA2695A775D582D8B40B7DBA5611"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7404666/pdf/AAS-9999-na.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/172185358/aas.13673.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Centre for Research in Intensive Care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of C