ukakos","name":"Yannoukakos, Drakoulis","rank":94,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"73","first":"Georgia","key":"chenevixtrenchgeorgiapau","last":"Chenevix-Trench","name":"Chenevix-Trench, Georgia","rank":95,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"52","first":"Thomas A.","key":"sellersthomasapau","last":"Sellers","name":"Sellers, Thomas A.","rank":96,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Paul D.P.","key":"pharoahpauldppau","last":"Pharoah","name":"Pharoah, Paul D.P.","rank":97,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wei","key":"zhengweipau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Wei","rank":98,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jirong","key":"longjirongpau","last":"Long","name":"Long, Jirong","rank":99,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30559148"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1158/0008-5472.can-18-2726","issn":["00085472","05766656"],"issn_org":["00085472"],"issue":"3","journal":"Cancer Research","pages":"505-517","status":"p","title":"Cancer Research","volume":"79"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060947651"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fc276018-617b-4187-ad7b-494cfc921c05"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genetic data from nearly 63,000 women of European descent predicts DNA methylation biomarkers and epithelial ovarian cancer risk","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-543962","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: PET/MRI was introduced for clinical use in 2011 and is now an established modality for the imaging of brain and certain pelvic cancers, whereas clinical use for the imaging of other forms of cancer is not yet widespread. We therefore systematically investigated what has been published on the use of PET/MRI compared to PET/CT in the imaging of cancers outside the brain, focusing on clinical areas of application related to diagnosis, staging and restaging. METHODS: A systematic search of PubMed/MEDLINE, Embase and the Cochrane Library was performed. Studies evaluating the diagnostic performance of simultaneous PET/MRI in cancer patients were chosen. RESULTS: A total of 3,138 publications were identified and 116 published during the period 2012-2018 were included and were grouped according to the major cancer forms: 13 head and neck (HNC), 9 breast (BC), 21 prostate (PC), 14 gynaecological, 13 gastrointestinal (GIC), and 46 various cancers. Data from studies comparing PET/MRI and PET/CT for staging/restaging suggested the superiority of 18F-FDG PET/MRI for the detection of tumour extension and retropharyngeal lymph node metastases in nasopharyngeal cancer, and for the detection of liver metastases and possibly bone marrow metastases in high-risk BC. FDG PET/MRI tended to be inferior for the detection of lung metastases in HNC and BC. 68Ga-PSMA-11 PET/MRI was superior to PET/CT for the detection of local PC recurrence. FDG PET/MRI was superior to FDG PET/CT for the detection of local tumour invasion in cervical cancer and had higher accuracy for the detection of liver metastases in colorectal cancer. CONCLUSION: The scoping review methodology resulted in the identification of a huge number of records, of which less than 5% were suitable for inclusion and only a limited number allowed conclusions on the advantages/disadvantages of PET/MRI compared to PET/CT in the oncological setting. There was evidence to support the use of FDG PET/MRI in staging of nasopharyngeal cancer and high-risk BC. Preliminary data indicate the superiority of PET/MRI for the detection of local recurrence in PC, local tumour invasion in cervical cancer, and liver metastases in colorectal cancer. These conclusions are based on small datasets and need to be further explored.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Morsing, Anni","Hildebrandt, Malene Grubbe","Vilstrup, Mie Holm","Dahlsgaard-Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth","Gerke, Oke","Petersen, Henrik","Johansen, Allan","Andersen, Thomas Lund","Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-627312"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["F FDG","Oncology","PET CT","PET MRI","Staging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hybrid pet mri in major cancers a scoping review","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151944864/EJNM_D_19_00325_R1_SDU_homepage.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-627312","identifier":[{"id":"31267161","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85068748562","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-bcb3558f-2726-4e80-afd8-f995998f19f5"],"keyword":["F-FDG","Oncology","PET/CT","PET/MRI","Staging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4D3D428698BA389F006834346FCB8CF2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151944864/EJNM_D_19_00325_R1_SDU_homepage.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anni","key":"morsingpau","last":"Morsing","locid":"eb322987-0180-4887-8e6c-9c9cb4f6ef39","name":"Morsing, Anni","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Grubbe","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"89ec551d-ddfe-45e8-983a-f2bbc54f8a0e","name":"Hildebrandt, Malene Grubbe","orcid":"0000-0003-2720-9018","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mie Holm","key":"vilstruppau","last":"Vilstrup","locid":"9ceb6215-deb0-460f-8c59-bbc32b7dca27","name":"Vilstrup, Mie Holm","orcid":"0000-0002-4760-0068","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Elisabeth","key":"walleniuspau","last":"Wallenius","locid":"09dbda03-897a-47e9-8ce4-7c2e523c417c","name":"Dahlsgaard-Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth","name_org":"Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oke","key":"gerkepau","last":"Gerke","locid":"596baeb1-6754-4d53-948f-30470dd1d976","name":"Gerke, Oke","orcid":"0000-0001-6335-3303","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"ea635371-4294-4379-9655-3da538fecf13","name":"Petersen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-1118-1500","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"dc7a1a61-b703-48ec-bd87-c92b55784133","name":"Johansen, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-057X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Lund","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8a904314-798c-4e45-9559-b997a4e1d5c7","name":"Andersen, Thomas Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-2860-6317","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Poul Flemming","key":"høilundcarlsenpau","last":"Høilund-Carlsen","locid":"a1ff65cf-cdaa-4192-bef3-a915cfe6cceb","name":"Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming","orcid":"0000-0001-7420-2367","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31267161"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00259-019-04402-8","issn":["16197070","16197089"],"issn_org":["16197070"],"issue":"10","journal":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","pages":"2138-2151","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068748562"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bcb3558f-2726-4e80-afd8-f995998f19f5"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Hybrid PET/MRI in major cancers : a scoping review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-627312","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Delirium among patients in the intensive care unit (ICU) is a common condition associated with increased morbidity and mortality. Haloperidol is the most frequently used pharmacologic intervention, but its use is not supported by firm evidence. Therefore, we are conducting Agents Intervening against Delirium in the Intensive Care Unit (AID-ICU) trial to assess the benefits and harms of haloperidol for the treatment of ICU-acquired delirium. METHODS: AID-ICU is an investigator-initiated, pragmatic, international, randomised, blinded, parallel-group, trial allocating adult ICU patients with manifest delirium 1:1 to haloperidol or placebo. Trial participants will receive intravenous 2.5 mg haloperidol three times daily or matching placebo (isotonic saline 0.9%) if they are delirious. If needed, a maximum of 20 mg/daily haloperidol/placebo is given. An escape protocol, not including haloperidol, is part of the trial protocol. The primary outcome is days alive out of the hospital within 90 days post-randomisation. Secondary outcomes are number of days without delirium or coma, serious adverse reactions to haloperidol, usage of escape medication, number of days alive without mechanical ventilation; mortality, health-related quality-of-life and cognitive function at 1-year follow-up. A sample size of 1000 patients is required to detect a 7-day improvement or worsening of the mean days alive out of the hospital, type 1 error risk of 5% and power 90%. PERSPECTIVE: The AID-ICU trial is based on gold standard methodology applied to a large sample of clinically representative patients and will provide pivotal high-quality data on the benefits and harms of haloperidol for the treatment ICU-acquired delirium.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Andersen-Ranberg, Nina C","Poulsen, Lone M","Perner, Anders","Wetterslev, Jørn","Estrup, Stine","Lange, Theis","Ebdrup, Bjørn H","Hästbacka, Johanna","Morgan, Matthew P G","Citerio, Giuseppe","Zafrani, Lara","Caballero, Jesús","Oxenbøll-Collet, Marie","Weber, Sven-Olaf","Andreasen, Anne S","Bestle, Morten","Pedersen, Helle B S","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Thee, Carsten","Jensen, Troels B","Dey, Nilanjan","Nielsen, Louise G","Mathiesen, Ole"],"cuid":["S04-095.23-011140"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","France","Italy","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["AP-HP Assistance Publique - Hopitaux de Paris","All Global Affiliations","Assistance publique – Hôpitaux de Paris","Autonomous University of Barcelona","Helsinki University Hospital","Service d'Hématologie adulte et Centre d'Investigation Clinique Hôpital Saint Louis, Paris, France","University of Helsinki","University of Milan - Bicocca","University of Milano-Bicocca","University of Wales"],"keyword":["Antipsychotics","Delirium","Haloperidol","ICU","Intensive care unit","delirium treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Adult Critical Care, University of Wales, Cardiff, Wales, UK."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"agents intervening against delirium in the intensive care unit aid icu protocol for a randomised placebo controlled trial of haloperidol in patients with delirium in the icu","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/249438077/Agents_Intervening_against_Delirium_in_the_Intensive_Care_