search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","collaboration for research in intensive care"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e9175c35-9557-4465-bac9-426c7123730f","au-f14b77b8-0fc8-4d53-9680-0e1f9110ea40","ku-37d342c5-d3b8-462b-8ed0-7100d27a1e13","sdu-3c0d1f46-b229-42a1-9d37-75e2ca117dbb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Agents Intervening against Delirium in the Intensive Care Unit (AID-ICU) - Protocol for a randomised placebo-controlled trial of haloperidol in patients with delirium in the ICU","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-095.23-011140","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Enterprise computing applications generally consists of several inter-related business processes linked together via shared data objects and events. We address the open challenge of providing formal modelling and implementation techniques for such enterprise computing applications, introducing the declarative, data-centric and event-driven process language RESEDA for REactive SEmi-structured DAta. The language is inspired by the computational model of spreadsheets and recent advances in declarative business process modelling notations. The key idea is to associate either input events or reactive computation events to the individual elements of semi-structured data and declare reactive behaviour as explicit reaction rules and constraints between these events. Moreover, RESEDA comes with a formal operational semantics given as rewrite rules supporting both formal analysis and persistent execution of the application as sequences of rewrites of the data. The data, along with the set of constraints, thereby at the same time constitutes the specification of the data, its behaviour and the run-time execution component. This key contribution of the paper is to introduce the RESEDA language, its formal execution semantics and give a sufficient condition for liveness of programs. We also establish Turing-equivalence of the language independently of the choice of underlying data expressions and exemplify the use of RESEDA by a running example of an online store. A prototype implementation of RESEDA and the examples of the paper are available on-line at http://dcr.tools/reseda.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Costa Seco, Joao","Debois, Soren","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S02-093.42-038320"],"event":{"acronym":"EDOC","end":"2018-10-19","place":"Stockholm, se","start":"2018-10-16","title":"22nd IEEE International Enterprise Distributed Object Computing Conference, EDOC 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Data Centric Systems","Declarative Process Modelling","Enterprise Computing","Event Driven Architecture","Formal Operational Semantics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reseda declaring live event driven computations as reactive semi structured data","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83725104/preprint_reseda.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-093.42-038320","identifier":[{"id":"85059070899","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-70171fa5-b057-411e-a63c-46185ecc9c90","ku-9dc7884b-f9a4-4a45-8af1-9810c8789435"],"keyword":["Data-Centric Systems","Declarative Process Modelling","Enterprise Computing","Event-Driven Architecture","Formal Operational Semantics","declarative, event-driven computations, semi structured data, liveness, enterprise applications, business processes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-344C0267D2F4817CC7C62DE4D3D4BC93"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83725104/preprint_reseda.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing Section","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"João Costa","key":"secopau","last":"Seco","name":"Seco, João Costa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Joao","key":"costasecopau","last":"Costa Seco","name":"Costa Seco, Joao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/edoc.2018.00020","eisbn":["9781538641392"],"isbn":["9781538641408"],"pages":"75-84","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2018 IEEE 22nd International Enterprise Distributed Object Computing Conference (EDOC)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059070899"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-70171fa5-b057-411e-a63c-46185ecc9c90","ku-9dc7884b-f9a4-4a45-8af1-9810c8789435"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"RESEDA: Declaring Live Event-Driven Computations as REactive SEmi-Structured DAta","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.42-038320","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"While the understandability of process models has been extensively investigated for different process modeling notations, it has not been yet broadened to cover hybrid models. This paper proposes a new research model to investigate the understandability of hybrid model representations using a variety of psycho-physiological measurements including eye tracking and galvanic skin response (GSR) together with verbal data analysis. The aim of this research is to ensure a smooth integration of hybrid modelling technologies in public administrations by investigating the way end-users (i.e., case workers) rely on the different parts of the hybrid process model representation in DCR Graphs, i.e., the graph, the textual annotations describing the law, and the simulation tools to interpret the process model.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Abbad Andaloussi, Amine","Slaats, Tijs","Burattin, Andrea","Hildebrandt, Thomas Troels","Weber, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-373149"],"event":{"acronym":"CaiSE","end":"2018-06-15","place":"Tallinn, ee","start":"2018-06-11","title":"30th International Conference on Advanced Information Systems Engineering","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"understandability of hybrid process models using dcr graphs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/149169776/UnderstandabilityPP.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-373149","ids":["dtu-e57f34b9-e1eb-4a6b-93fc-861cd048f336"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CD0087FB9B412C6599AD086002B0D991"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/149169776/UnderstandabilityPP.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Software and Process Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amine","key":"abbadandaloussipau","last":"Abbad Andaloussi","locid":"ec567f0e-aa1c-42e2-a523-fccf2f03efbe","name":"Abbad Andaloussi, Amine","orcid":"0000-0002-3404-7849","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andrea","key":"burattinpau","last":"Burattin","locid":"75b43f3c-f477-4ac8-8717-c6d2b93bed02","name":"Burattin, Andrea","orcid":"0000-0002-0837-0183","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Troels","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas Troels","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Barbara","key":"weberpau","last":"Weber","locid":"4bbfa31e-3aa1-4565-88b1-8c19946807e6","name":"Weber, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-6004-4860","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 30th International Conference on Advanced Information Systems Engineering"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e57f34b9-e1eb-4a6b-93fc-861cd048f336"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Understandability of Hybrid Process Models Using DCR Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-373149","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Large-scale genome-wide association studies (GWAS) have identified approximately 35 loci associated with epithelial ovarian cancer (EOC) risk. The majority of GWAS-identified disease susceptibility variants are located in noncoding regions, and causal genes underlying these associations remain largely unknown. Here, we performed a transcriptome-wide association study to search for novel genetic loci and plausible causal genes at known GWAS loci. We used RNA sequencing data (68 normal ovarian tissue samples from 68 individuals and 6,124 cross-tissue samples from 369 individuals) and high-density genotyping data from European descendants of the Genotype-Tissue Expression (GTEx V6) project to build ovarian and cross-tissue models of genetically regulated expression using elastic net methods. We evaluated 17,121 genes for their cis-predicted gene expression in relation to EOC risk using summary statistics data from GWAS of 97,898 women, including 29,396 EOC cases. With a Bonferroni-corrected significance level of P < 2.2 × 10-6, we identified 35 genes, including FZD4 at 11q14.2 (Z = 5.08, P = 3.83 × 10-7, the cross-tissue model; 1 Mb away from any GWAS-identified EOC risk variant), a potential novel locus for EOC risk. All other 34 significantly associated genes were located within 1 Mb of known GWAS-identified loci, including 23 genes at 6 loci not previously linked to EOC risk. Upon conditioning on nearby known EOC GWAS-identified variants, the associations for 31 genes disappeared and three genes remained (P < 1.47 × 10-3). These data identify one novel locus (FZD4) and 34 genes at 13 known EOC risk loci associated with EOC risk, providing new insights into EOC carcinogenesis.Significance: Transcriptomic analysis of a large cohort confirms earlier GWAS loci and reveals FZD4 as a novel locus associated with EOC risk. Cancer Res; 78(18); 5419-30. ©2018 AACR.","author_count":144,"contributors":["Lu, Yingchang","Beeghly-Fadiel, Alicia","Wu, Lang","Guo, Xingyi","Li, Bingshan","Schildkraut, Joellen M","Im, Hae Kyung","Chen, Yian A","Permuth, Jennifer B","Reid, Brett M","Teer, Jamie K","Moysich, Kirsten B","Andrulis, Irene L","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Arun, Banu K","Bandera, Elisa V","Barkardottir, Rosa B","Barnes, Daniel R","Benitez, Javier","Bjorge, Line","Brenton, James","Butzow, Ralf","Caldes, Trinidad","Caligo, Maria A","Campbell, Ian","Chang-Claude, Jenny","Claes, Kathleen B M","Couch, Fergus J","Cramer, Daniel W","Daly, Mary B","deFazio, Anna","Dennis, Joe","Diez, Orland","Domchek, Susan M","Dörk, Thilo","Easton, Douglas F","Eccles, Diana M","Fasching, Peter A","Fortner, Renée T","Fountzilas, George","Friedman, Eitan","Ganz, Patricia A","Garber, Judy","Giles, Graham G","Godwin, Andrew K","Goldgar, David E","Goodman, Marc T","Greene, Mark H","Gronwald, Jacek","Hamann, Ute","Heitz, Florian","Hildebrandt, Michelle A T","Høgdall, Claus K","Hollestelle, Antoinette","Hulick, Peter J","Huntsman, David G","Imyanitov, Evgeny N","Isaacs, Claudine","Jakubowska, Anna","James, Paul","Karlan, Beth Y","Kelemen, Linda E","Kiemeney, Lambertus A","Kjaer, Susanne K","Kwong, Ava","Le, Nhu D","Leslie, Goska","Lesueur, Fabienne","Levine, Douglas A","Mattiello, Amalia","May, Taymaa","McGuffog, Lesley","McNeish, Iain A","Merritt, Melissa A","Modugno, Francesmary","Montagna, Marco","Neuhausen, Susan L","Nevanlinna, Heli","Nielsen, Finn C","Nikitina-Zake, Liene","Nussbaum, Robert L","Offit, Kenneth","Olah, Edith","Olopade, Olufunmilayo I","Olson, Sara H","Olsson, Håkan","Osorio, Ana","Park, Sue K","Parsons, Michael T","Peeters, Petra H M","Pejovic, Tanja","Peterlongo, Paolo","Phelan, Catherine M","Pujana, Miquel Angel","Ramus, Susan J","Rennert, Gad","Risch, Harvey","Rodriguez, Gustavo C","Rodríguez-Antona, Cristina","Romieu, Isabelle","Rookus, Matti A","Rossing, Mary Anne","Rzepecka, Iwona K","Sandler, Dale P","Schmutzler, Rita K","Setiawan, Veronica W","Sharma, Priyanka","Sieh, Weiva","Simard, Jacques","Singer, Christian F","Song, Honglin","S