{"abstract":"We describe how the declarative Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) Graphs proces notation can be used to digitalise the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and make a first evaluation to what extend the formalisation and associated tool for end-user modelling and simulation can be used to clarify the meaning of the GDPR and its consequences for the main business process of a Danish funding agency.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Heuck, Emil","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Kiærulff Lerche, Rasmus","Marquard, Morten","Normann, Håkon","Iven Strømsted, Rasmus","Weber, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-378879"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-15","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2017-09-10","title":"15th International Conference on Business Process Management","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["DCR Graphs","Formalisation","GDPR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digitalising the general data protection regulation with dynamic condition response graphs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/141007594/BPM17industry12.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-378879","identifier":[{"id":"85035045471","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f86061bb-b7ce-4f0b-813f-439cacb2ee61"],"keyword":["DCR Graphs","Formalisation","GDPR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2F05185BF1CFA975A268E3B45F9D1EE7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/141007594/BPM17industry12.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1