{"abstract":"The DCR Workbench is an online tool for simulation and analysis of collaborative distributed processes specified as DCR graphs. The Workbench is a robust and comprehensive implementation of DCR graphs, providing concrete syntax, specification by refinement, visualisation, simulation, static analysis, time analysis, enforcement, declarative subprocesses, data dependencies, translation to other declarative models, and more. This chapter introduces the Workbench and, through the features of the Workbench, surveys the DCR formalism. The Workbench is available on-line at http: //dcr.tools.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383270"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collaborative distributed processes","DCR Graphs","DCR Workbench","Data dependencies","Declarative subprocesses","Formal specification","Simulation and analysis","Static analysis","Time analysis","Visualisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the dcr workbench declarative choreographies for collaborative processes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.riverpublishers.com/pdf/ebook/chapter/RP_9788793519817C5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383270","identifier":[{"id":"85053613034","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-88834914-a51b-49fb-ae54-c06a45d5d2e5"],"keyword":["Collaborative distributed processes","DCR Workbench","DCR graphs","Data dependencies","Declarative subprocesses","Formal specification","Simulation and analysis","Static analysis","Time analysis","Visualisation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-0A6905B80B7FA3B5A431983E819FB9E9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.riverpublishers.com/pdf/ebook/chapter/RP_9788793519817C5.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Simon","key":"gaypedh","last":"Gay","name":"Gay, Simon","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"António","key":"ravarapedh","last":"Ravara","name":"Ravara, António","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793519824"],"issn":["00010782"],"pages":"99-124","publisher":"River Publishers","series":"River Publishers Series in Automation, Control and Robotics","status":"p","title":"Behavioural Types: from Theory to Tools"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053613034"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-88834914-a51b-49fb-ae54-c06a45d5d2e5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The DCR Workbench: Declarative Choreographies for Collaborative Processes","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383270","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Based on ethnographic fieldwork, and the modelling of work processes at a medical department, this paper considers some of the opportunities and challenges involved in working with models in a complex work setting. The paper introduces a flexible modelling tool to CSCW, called the DCR Portal, and considers how it may be used to model complex work settings collaboratively. Further, the paper discusses how models created with the DCR portal may potentially play a key role in making a cooperative work ensemble appreciate, discuss and coordinate key interdependencies inherent to their cooperative work practices.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars Rune","Hildebrandt, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383602"],"event":{"acronym":"C&T","title":"International Conference on Communities and Technologies"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CSCW","Collaborative Work Practices","DCR Portal","Ethnographic fieldwork","Work Process Modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling cooperative work at a medical department","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83457483/Christensen_Hildebrandt_2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383602","identifier":[{"id":"85025121871","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a0682094-ae95-4249-ba2b-007adbd9eef4"],"keyword":["CSCW","Collaborative Work Practices","DCR Portal","Ethnographic Fieldwork","Work Process Modelling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3F13D79A2B3B117C140F0D09C29EBF7D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83457483/Christensen_Hildebrandt_2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3083671.3083682","isbn":["9781450348546"],"pages":"46-55","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"C&amp;T '17 Proceedings of the 8th International Conference on Communities and Technologies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025121871"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a0682094-ae95-4249-ba2b-007adbd9eef4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modelling Cooperative Work at a Medical Department","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383602","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) have identified 18 loci associated with serous ovarian cancer (SOC) susceptibility but the biological mechanisms driving these findings remain poorly characterised. Germline cancer risk loci may be enriched for target genes of transcription factors (TFs) critical to somatic tumorigenesis. METHODS: All 615 TF-target sets from the Molecular Signatures Database were evaluated using gene set enrichment analysis (GSEA) and three GWAS for SOC risk: discovery (2196 cases/4396 controls), replication (7035 cases/21 693 controls; independent from discovery), and combined (9627 cases/30 845 controls; including additional individuals). RESULTS: The PAX8-target gene set was ranked 1/615 in the discovery (PGSEA<0.001; FDR=0.21), 7/615 in the replication (PGSEA=0.004; FDR=0.37), and 1/615 in the combined (PGSEA<0.001; FDR=0.21) studies. Adding other genes reported to interact with PAX8 in the literature to the PAX8-target set and applying an alternative to GSEA, interval enrichment, further confirmed this association (P=0.006). Fifteen of the 157 genes from this expanded PAX8 pathway were near eight loci associated with SOC risk at P<10(-5) (including six with P<5 × 10(-8)). The pathway was also associated with differential gene expression after shRNA-mediated silencing of PAX8 in HeyA8 (PGSEA=0.025) and IGROV1 (PGSEA=0.004) SOC cells and several PAX8 targets near SOC risk loci demonstrated in vitro transcriptomic perturbation. CONCLUSIONS: Putative PAX8 target genes are enriched for common SOC risk variants. This finding from our agnostic evaluation is of particular interest given that PAX8 is well-established as a specific marker for the cell of origin of SOC.","author_count":86,"contributors":["Kar, Siddhartha P","Adler, Emily","Tyrer, Jonathan","Hazelett, Dennis","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Bandera, Elisa V","Beckmann, Matthias W","Berchuck, Andrew","Bogdanova, Natalia","Brinton, Louise","Butzow, Ralf","Campbell, Ian","Carty, Karen","Chang-Claude, Jenny","Cook, Linda S","Cramer, Daniel W","Cunningham, Julie M","Dansonka-Mieszkowska, Agnieszka","Doherty, Jennifer Anne","Dörk, Thilo","Dürst, Matthias","Eccles, Diana","Fasching, Peter A","Flanagan, James","Gentry-Maharaj, Aleksandra","Glasspool, Rosalind","Goode, Ellen L","Goodman, Marc T","Gronwald, Jacek","Heitz, Florian","Hildebrandt, Michelle A T","Høgdall, Estrid","Høgdall, Claus","Huntsman, David G","Jensen, Allan","Karlan, Beth Y","Kelemen, Linda E","Kiemeney, Lambertus A","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Kupryjanczyk, Jolanta","Lambrechts, Diether","Levine, Douglas A","Li, Qiyuan","Lissowska, Jolanta","Lu, Karen H","Lubiński, Jan","Massuger, Leon F A G","McGuire, Valerie","McNeish, Iain","Menon, Usha","Modugno, Francesmary","Monteiro, Alvaro N","Moysich, Kirsten B","Ness, Roberta B","Nevanlinna, Heli","Paul, James","Pearce, Celeste L","Pejovic, Tanja","Permuth, Jennifer B","Phelan, Catherine","Pike, Malcolm C","Poole, Elizabeth M","Ramus, Susan J","Risch, Harvey A","Rossing, Mary Anne","Salvesen, Helga B","Schildkraut, Joellen M","Sellers, Thomas A","Sherman, Mark","Siddiqui, Nadeem","Sieh, Weiva","Song, Honglin","Southey, Melissa","Terry, Kathryn L","Tworoger, Shelley S","Walsh, Christine","Wentzensen, Nicolas","Whittemore, Alice S","Wu, Anna H","Yang, Hannah","Zheng, Wei","Ziogas, Argyrios","Freedman, Matthew L","Gayther, Simon A","Pharoah, Paul D P","Lawrenson, Kate"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-395346"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Case Control Studies","Cell Line Tumor","Cell Transformation Neoplastic","Cystadenocarcinoma Serous","Female","Gene Amplification","Gene Expression Profiling","Gene Expression Regulation Neoplastic","Genetic Loci","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome Wide Association Study","Humans","Journal Article","Meta Analysis as Topic","Microarray Analysis","Neoplasms Glandular and Epithelial","Ovarian Neoplasms","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enrichment of putative pax000000000008 target genes at serous epithelial ovarian cancer susceptibility loci","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/bjc.2016.426","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-395346","identifier":[{"id":"28103614","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5318969","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85010004839","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-03299208-9028-40c1-966d-2ade1d86e282"],"keyword":["Case-Control Studies","Cell Line, Tumor","Cell Transformation, Neoplastic","Cystadenocarcinoma, Serous","Female","Gene Amplification","Gene Expression Profiling","Gene Expression Regulation, Neoplastic","Genetic Loci","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome-Wide Association Study","Humans","Journal Article","Meta-Analysis as Topic","Microarray Analysis","Neoplasms, Glandular and Epithelial","Ovarian Neoplasms","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B6B8320DCD96E9F437CD791E271FE4B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/203454162/bjc2016426.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/bjc.2016.426","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet,