l ovarian cancer susceptibility loci","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-395346","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"(a)Situation faced: Exformatics, a Danish adaptive case-management vendor, wanted to leverage declarative process tools to support the flexible processes found at BRFkredit. However, switching from the more common flow-based notations to a declarative notation brought new challenges in terms of understandability. We undertook the project described in this chapter to investigate and address these challenges. (b)Action taken: We started our investigation by having several full-day and half-day meetings to discuss BRFkredit’s requirements. Based on these requirements, we proposed and developed a prototype hybrid process-modelling approach with which models are defined declaratively, but the possible behavior of the model can be viewed and investigated using flow-based notions. The prototype was then presented to BRFkredit for feedback. (c)Results achieved: Our investigation helped to clarify the requirements for making declarative process models understandable to end users at BRFkredit and showed how a hybrid approach could be used to satisfy these requirements. Based on these insights, we developed tools to enhance our existing declarative modelling framework with flow-based visualizations. (d)Lessons learned: Different stakeholders have different needs and preferred levels of abstraction when process models are used as tools for communication. However, one model that seems to fit most situations is a simple no-branches sequential swimlane diagram that was extracted automatically from a more detailed declarative model. These observations enabled Exformatics to enhance its declarative modelling framework to make it more attractive to end-users.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Marquard, Morten","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038329"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adaptive Case Management","Declarative process models","Flow based visualizations","Hybrid process modelling","User requirements in process modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hybrid process technologies in the financial sector the case of brfkredit","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442971/final_published.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-038329","identifier":[{"id":"85041698110","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-765aee03-c92a-447e-9707-f20e4db7fbfe","ku-46063302-61f0-44e0-9061-917eab77de39"],"keyword":["Adaptive case management","Declarative process models","Flow-based visualizations","Hybrid process-modelling","User requirements in process modelling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-11EE05BA16DAB980AD82ECDC70E2AF9B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442971/final_published.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"marquardpau","last":"Marquard","name":"Marquard, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-58307-5_21","eisbn":["9783319583075"],"isbn":["9783319583068"],"issn":["2192810X"],"pages":"397-412","publisher":"Springer","series":"Management for Professionals","status":"p","subtitle":"Digital Innovation and Business Transformation in Practice","title":"Business Process Management Cases"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041698110"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-765aee03-c92a-447e-9707-f20e4db7fbfe","ku-46063302-61f0-44e0-9061-917eab77de39"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hybrid Process Technologies in the Financial Sector : The Case of BRFkredit","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038329","year":"2017","yearsub":2019}
{"abstract":"We present the first session typing system guaranteeing request-response liveness properties for possibly non-terminating communicating processes. The types augment the branch and select types of the standard binary session types with a set of required responses, indicating that whenever a particular label is selected, a set of other labels, its responses, must eventually also be selected. We prove that these extended types are strictly more expressive than standard session types. We provide a type system for a process calculus similar to a subset of collaborative BPMN processes with internal (data-based) and external (event-based) branching, message passing, bounded and unbounded looping. We prove that this type system is sound, i.e., it guarantees request-response liveness for dead-lock free processes. We exemplify the use of the calculus and type system on a concrete example of an infinite state system.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Slaats, Tijs","Yoshida, Nobuko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384582"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London"],"keyword":["Bounded recursion","Business processes","Liveness","Process algebra","Session types","Typing system"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Exformatics"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"type checking liveness for collaborative processes with bounded and unbounded recursion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2168/LMCS-12(1:1)2016","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384582","identifier":[{"id":"84960154263","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e12b68e9-0f86-4eb2-b756-d04c028ce72b"],"keyword":["Bounded recursion","Business processes","Liveness","Process algebra","Session types","Typing system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9486547B25609DB604C1BC2D3C25C59A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2168/LMCS-12(1:1)2016","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1510.06658v2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Exformatics"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nobuko","key":"yoshidapau","last":"Yoshida","name":"Yoshida, Nobuko","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2168/lmcs-12(1:1)2016","issn":["18605974"],"issue":"1","journal":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","pages":"1-38","publisher":"International Federation for Computational Logic","status":"p","title":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960154263"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e12b68e9-0f86-4eb2-b756-d04c028ce72b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Type-checking Liveness for Collaborative Processes with Bounded and Unbounded Recursion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384582","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we present a direct algorithm for session type inference for the π-calculus. Type inference for session types has previously been achieved by either imposing limitations and restriction on the π-calculus, or by reducing the type inference problem to that for linear types. Our approach is based on constraint generation and solving. We generate constraints for a process based on its syntactical components, and afterwards solve the generated constraints in a predetermined order. We prove the soundness, completeness, and termination of this approach.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Graversen, Eva Fajstrup","Harbo, Jacob Buchreitz","Hüttel, Hans","Bjerregaard, Mathias Ormstrup","Poulsen, Niels Sonnich","Wahl, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-120790"],"event":{"end":"2014-09-12","place":"Eindhoven, nl","start":"2014-09-11","title":"11th International Workshop: FASOCC","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"type inference for session types in the pi calculus","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://wsfm2014.haifa.ac.il/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-120790","identifier":[{"id":"84964793088","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f34629b3-6a70-4a7a-9526-a644ae96d417"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B3504BBF4F0255CD86BEBF70E530A6D"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Fajstrup","key":"graversenpau","last":"Graversen","locid":"19610a8d-9440-48ca-9e48-25bd4ed07bdb","name":"Graversen, Eva Fajstrup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Buchreitz","key":"harbopau","last":"Harbo","locid":"938b8f8c-71e2-4c96-8284-83c4b94893c3","name":"Harbo, Jacob Buchreitz","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"huttelpau","last":"Huttel","locid":"374c283d-9961-4b1a-9fbd-77b4fa0dc30d","name":"Hüttel, Hans","name_org":"Huttel, Hans","orcid":"0000-0002-4603-5407","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathias Ormstrup","key":"bjerregaardpau","last":"Bjerregaard","locid":"bf388dfa-f0e8-4da2-b1a1-9e0678685dd1","name":"Bjerregaard, Mathias Ormstrup","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Sonnich","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"82477b90-f50a-4e00-ac52-cf6dfc326d2d","name":"Poulsen, Niels Sonnich","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"wahlpau","last":"Wahl","locid":"f4e28ed7-81f7-49ba-b744-df8ac0bc55d3","name":"Wahl, Sebastian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpedh","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"António","key":"ravarapedh","last":"Ravara","name":"Ravara, António","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan Martijn","key":"vanderwerfpedh","last":"van der Werf","name":"van der Werf, Jan Martijn","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mathias","key":"weidlichpedh","last":"Weidlich","name":"Weidlich, Mathias","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-33612-1_7","eisbn":["9783319336121"],"isbn":["9783319336114"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"103-121","place":"Heidelberg","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"11th International Workshop, WS-FM 2014, Eindhoven, The Netherlands, September 11-12, 2014, and 12th International Workshop, WS-FM/BEAT 2015, Madrid, Spain, September 4-5, 2015, Revised Selected Papers","title":"Web Services, Formal Methods, and Behavioral Types"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964793088"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f34629b3-6a70-4a7a-9526-a644ae96d417"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Type Inference for Session Types in the Pi-Calculus","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-120790","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"An expert system is a computer system for inferring knowledge from a knowledge base, typically by using a set of inference rules. When the concept of expert systems was introduced at Stanford University in the early 1970s, the knowledge base was an unstructured set of facts. Today the knowledge base of expert systems is often given in terms of an ontology, extracted and built from various data sources by employing natural language-processing and statistics. To emphasize such capabilities, the term “expert” is now often replaced by “cognitive,” “knowledge,” “knowledge-based,” or “intelligent” system. With very few exceptions, general-purpose expert systems have failed to emerge so far. However, expert systems are applied in specialized domains, particularly in healthcare. The increasing availability of large quantities of data to organizations today provides a valuable opportunity for the application of expert systems, but also raises issues regarding privacy and legal liability.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Thomas Troels","Cattani, Gian Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384476"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","MAPS Società per Azioni (SPA)"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Communication theory","Computer Science","Data mining","Human Computer Interaction"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"expert system","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384476","ids":["itu-da166bf3-e02f-4ee9-a36e-e695d1053ae1"],"keyword":["artificial intelligence","communication theory","computer science","data-mining","human-computer interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7824B76A07DBFDDACE395170BBEC7C6C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"maps società per azioni","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"MAPS Società per Azioni (SPA)","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Troels","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas Troels","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gian Luca","key":"cattanipau","last":"Cattani","name":"Cattani, Gian Luca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus Bruhn","key":"jensenpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Klaus Bruhn","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Robert T.","key":"craigpedh","last":"Craig","name":"Craig, Robert T.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jefferson D.","key":"pooleypedh","last":"Pooley","name":"Pooley, Jefferson D.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eric W.","key":"rothenbuhlerpedh","last":"Rothenbuhler","name":"Rothenbuhler, Eric W.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/9781118766804.wbiect244","eisbn":["9781118766804"],"publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","series":"The Wiley Blackwell-ICA International Encyclopedias of Communication","status":"p","title":"The International Encyclopedia of Communication Theory and Philosophy","volume":"1-4"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-da166bf3-e02f-4ee9-a36e-e695d1053ae1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Expert System","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384476","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Disruption in circadian gene expression, whether due to genetic variation or environmental factors (e.g., light at night, shiftwork), is associated with increased incidence of breast, prostate, gastrointestinal and hematologic cancers and gliomas. Circadian genes are highly expressed in the ovaries where they regulate ovulation; circadian disruption is associated with several ovarian cancer risk factors (e.g., endometriosis). However, no studies have examined variation in germline circadian genes as predictors of ovarian cancer risk and invasiveness. The goal of the current study was to examine single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) in circadian genes BMAL1, CRY2, CSNK1E, NPAS2, PER3, REV1 and TIMELESS and downstream transcription factors KLF10 and SENP3 as predictors of risk of epithelial ovarian cancer (EOC) and histopathologic subtypes. The study included a test set of 3,761 EOC cases and 2,722 controls and a validation set of 44,308 samples including 18,174 (10,316 serous) cases and 26,134 controls from 43 studies participating in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (OCAC). Analysis of genotype data from 36 genotyped SNPs and 4600 imputed SNPs indicated that the most significant association was rs117104877 in BMAL1 (OR = 0.79, 95% CI = 0.68-0.90, p = 5.59 × 10(-4)]. Functional analysis revealed a significant down regulation of BMAL1 expression following cMYC overexpression and increasing transformation in ovarian surface epithelial (OSE) cells as well as alternative splicing of BMAL1 exons in ovarian and granulosa cells. These results suggest that variation in circadian genes, and specifically BMAL1, may be associated with risk of ovarian cancer, likely through disruption of hormonal pathways.","author_count":155,"contributors":["Jim, Heather S L","Lin, Hui-Yi","Tyrer, Jonathan P","Lawrenson, Kate","Dennis, Joe","Chornokur, Ganna","Chen, Zhihua","Chen, Y Ann","Permuth-Wey, Jennifer","Aben, Katja Kh","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Antonenkova, Natalia",