{"abstract":"By trustworthy adaptive case management we mean that it should be possible to adapt processes and goals at runtime while guaranteeing that no deadlocks and livelocks are introduced. We propose to support this by applying a formal declarative process model, DCR Graphs, and exemplify its operational semantics that supports both run time changes and formal verification. We show how these techniques are being implemented in industry as a component of the Exformatics case management tools. Finally we discuss the planned future work, which will aim to allow changes to be tested for conformance wrt policies specified either as linear time logic (LTL) or DCR Graphs, extend the language with time and data and offer extended support for cross-organizational case management systems.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Mukkamala, Raghava Rao","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Slaats, Tijs","Marquard, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382688"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adaptive Case Management","Declarative Workflows","Dynamic Business Processes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Exformatics"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic condition response graphs for trustworthy adaptive case management","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://download.springer.com/static/pdf/705/chp%253A10.1007%252F978-3-642-41033-8_23.pdf?auth66=1387556746_487f3eb4053c2edf94e3eabd925d111a&ext=.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382688","identifier":[{"id":"84886740736","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5eb2a334-ce06-4f07-a70a-75f418ce42d3"],"keyword":["Adaptive Case Management","Declarative Workflows","Dynamic Business Processes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-777972CA2D7F7F085401334EE6D444E2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://download.springer.com/static/pdf/705/chp%253A10.1007%252F978-3-642-41033-8_23.pdf?auth66=1387556746_487f3eb4053c2edf94e3eabd925d111a&ext=.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Software & Systems","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Exformatics"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raghava Rao","key":"mukkamalapau","last":"Mukkamala","name":"Mukkamala, Raghava Rao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"marquardpau","last":"Marquard","name":"Marquard, Morten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783642410321"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"166-171","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"On the Move to Meaningful Internet Systems","volume":"8186"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84886740736"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5eb2a334-ce06-4f07-a70a-75f418ce42d3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dynamic Condition Response Graphs for Trustworthy Adaptive Case Management","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382688","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We describe how the declarative Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) Graphs process model can be used for trustworthy adaptive case management by leveraging the flexible execution, dynamic composition and adaptation supported by DCR Graphs. The dynamically composed and adapted graphs are verified for deadlock freedom and liveness in the SPIN model checker by utilizing a mapping from DCR Graphs to PROMELA code. We exemplify the approach by a small workflow extracted from a field study at a danish hospital.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Mukkamala, Raghava Rao","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381592"],"event":{"acronym":"EDOC","title":"IEEE International Enterprise Distributed Object Computing Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adaptive Case Management","Declarative Business Processes","Dynamic Business Processes","Verification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards trustworthy adaptive case management with dynamic condition response graphs","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/62413006/Adaptive_Case_Management_EDOC2013.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381592","identifier":[{"id":"84892489578","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-152e003f-a6e4-4b9a-8f41-0c2d4c1c60c9"],"keyword":["Adaptive Case Management","Declarative Business Processes","Dynamic Business Processes","verification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-85E75E7D1343D942CD3DB23D205B7C90"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/EDOC.2013.22","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/62413006/Adaptive_Case_Management_EDOC2013.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Software & Systems","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raghava Rao","key":"mukkamalapau","last":"Mukkamala","name":"Mukkamala, Raghava Rao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/edoc.2013.22","issn":["15417719"],"journal":"International Enterprise Distributed Object Computing Conference. Proceedings","pages":"127-136","status":"p","title":"International Enterprise Distributed Object Computing Conference. Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84892489578"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-152e003f-a6e4-4b9a-8f41-0c2d4c1c60c9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Trustworthy Adaptive Case Management with Dynamic Condition Response Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381592","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We conservatively extend the declarative Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) Graph process model, introduced in the PhD thesis of the second author, to allow for discrete time deadlines. We prove that safety and liveness properties can be verified by mapping finite timed DCR Graphs to finite state transition systems. We exemplify how deadlines can introduce time-locks and deadlocks and violate liveness. We then prove that the general technique for safe distribution of DCR Graphs provided in previous work can be extended to timed DCR Graphs. We exemplify the use of timed DCR Graphs and the distribution technique in praxis on a timed extension of a cross-organizational case management process arising from a previous case study. The example shows how a timed DCR Graph can be used to describe the global contract for a timed workflow process involving several organizations, which can then be distributed as a network of communicating timed DCR Graphs describing the local contract for each organization.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Thomas","Mukkamala, Raghava Rao","Slaats, Tijs","Zanitti, Francesco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383617"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Contracts","Cross organizational workflow","Declarative process models","Liveness","Safety","Time"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"contracts for cross organizational workflows as timed dynamic condition response graphs","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84891903707","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383617","identifier":[{"id":"84891903707","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a1a7a4b7-d555-4de8-9aaa-31d2c799af0b"],"keyword":["Contracts","Cross-organizational workflow","Declarative process models","Liveness","Safety","Time"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6ADD3AAC3DF2C9D3446BF914C36941B5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raghava Rao","key":"mukkamalapau","last":"Mukkamala","name":"Mukkamala, Raghava Rao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesco","key":"zanittipau","last":"Zanitti","name":"Zanitti, Francesco","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["23522208","23522216"],"issn_org":["23522208"],"journal":"Journal of Logic and Algebraic Programming","pages":"164-185","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Logic and Algebraic Programming","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a1a7a4b7-d555-4de8-9aaa-31d2c799af0b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Contracts for Cross-organizational Workflows as Timed Dynamic Condition Response Graphs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383617","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
