"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Trustworthy pervasive healthcare services via multiparty session types","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-524236","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Nephronophthisis is an autosomal recessive cystic kidney disease that leads to renal failure in childhood or adolescence. Most NPHP gene products form molecular networks. Here we identify ANKS6 as a new NPHP family member that connects NEK8 (NPHP9) to INVS (NPHP2) and NPHP3. We show that ANKS6 localizes to the proximal cilium and confirm its role in renal development through knockdown experiments in zebrafish and Xenopus laevis. We also identify six families with ANKS6 mutations affected by nephronophthisis, including severe cardiovascular abnormalities, liver fibrosis and situs inversus. The oxygen sensor HIF1AN hydroxylates ANKS6 and INVS and alters the composition of the ANKS6-INVS-NPHP3 module. Knockdown of Hif1an in Xenopus results in a phenotype that resembles loss of other NPHP proteins. Network analyses uncovered additional putative NPHP proteins and placed ANKS6 at the center of this NPHP module, explaining the overlapping disease manifestation caused by mutation in ANKS6, NEK8, INVS or NPHP3.","author_count":41,"contributors":["Hoff, Sylvia","Halbritter, Jan","Epting, Daniel","Frank, Valeska","Nguyen, Thanh-Minh T","van Reeuwijk, Jeroen","Boehlke, Christopher","Schell, Christoph","Yasunaga, Takayuki","Helmstädter, Martin","Mergen, Miriam","Filhol, Emilie","Boldt, Karsten","Horn, Nicola","Ueffing, Marius","Otto, Edgar A","Eisenberger, Tobias","Elting, Mariet W","van Wijk, Joanna A E","Bockenhauer, Detlef","Sebire, Neil J","Rittig, Søren","Vyberg, Mogens","Ring, Troels","Pohl, Martin","Pape, Lars","Neuhaus, Thomas J","Elshakhs, Neveen A Soliman","Koon, Sarah J","Harris, Peter C","Grahammer, Florian","Huber, Tobias B","Kuehn, E Wolfgang","Kramer-Zucker, Albrecht","Bolz, Hanno J","Roepman, Ronald","Saunier, Sophie","Walz, Gerd","Hildebrandt, Friedhelm","Bergmann, Carsten","Lienkamp, Soeren S"],"cuid":["S02-098.86-006817"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Freiburg"],"keyword":["Animals","Cilia","Consanguinity","Exons","Gene Knockdown Techniques","Humans","Introns","Kidney Diseases Cystic","Kinesin","Mice","Mutation","Nuclear Proteins","Phenotype","Polycystic Kidney Diseases","Protein Binding","Protein Interaction Maps","Protein Kinases","Protein Transport","Transcription Factors","Xenopus","Zebrafish","Zebrafish Proteins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anks000000000006 is a central component of a nephronophthisis module linking nek000000000008 to invs and nphp000000000003","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.2681","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.86-006817","identifier":[{"id":"23793029","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3786259","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84881028445","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000322374900023","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-8ca99593-de98-4fed-914e-dfa085ecd734","au-39dd210e-b4f2-4673-ac75-b0f585838b82"],"keyword":["Animals","Cilia","Consanguinity","Exons","Gene Knockdown Techniques","Humans","Introns","Kidney Diseases, Cystic","Kinesin","Mice","Mutation","Nuclear Proteins","Phenotype","Polycystic Kidney Diseases","Protein Binding","Protein Interaction Maps","Protein Kinases","Protein Transport","Transcription Factors","Xenopus","Zebrafish","Zebrafish Proteins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D6403700D0570815DBAE1D46A185ADE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.2681","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused"