{"abstract":"N,N' ,N'' -Trialkyltriazatriangulenium (R-TATA+) tetrafluoroborate (BF4) salts form highly ordered thin films directly when spin-cast onto rotating substrates. The homogeneous and crystalline thin films show macroscopic order over centimetres. The crystal structures of the R-TATA$BF4 salts are investigated and compared for the propyl, 3-methylpentyl and octyl derivatives. In all cases the molecules pack in hexagonally ordered bilayers, with segregation of the ionic groups and the alkyl chains. This is a rare packing motif with the rigid discotic TATA+ cores organized co-planarly in sheets separated by perpendicularly oriented alkyl chains, somewhat similar to a crystallized lamellar phase of phospholipid bilayers and the lamellar smectic mesophase of liquid crystals. The structure of the thin films is investigated by optical spectroscopy, X-ray reflectometry and grazing incidence X-ray diffraction. All techniques confirm that the 15–30 nm thick films maintain the lamellar structure of the bulk crystals, are flat on macroscopic length scales, and are completely ordered relative to the substrate. The triazatriangulenium molecules are electroactive dyes, and in the highly anisotropic polycrystalline thin film structure they show intense fluorescence and efficient exciton transport.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Just Sørensen, Thomas","Hildebrandt, Christoffer B.","Elm, Jonas","Andreasen, Jens Wenzel","Madsen, Anders Ø.","Westerlund, Frederik","Laursen, Bo W."],"cuid":["S02-092.50-036557"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Imaging and Structural Analysis"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"large area soft crystalline thin films of n n sup i sup n sup ii sup trialkyltriazatriangulenium salts with homeotropic alignment of the discotic cores in a lamellar lattice","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c2jm15954f","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.50-036557","identifier":[{"id":"84857525173","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-aef83e6f-fc0a-4215-9add-47913c77f3f6","ku-e906bf8b-b892-458c-9881-344cbdb55445"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B98B58D03B3D97CE32B3F931BED6BA5F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c2jm15954f","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage, Imaging and Structural Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Imaging and Structural Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Just","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"0744dbfc-1b71-4ed8-8fee-84ddc6005b6b","name":"Sørensen, Thomas Just","orcid":"0000-0003-1491-5116","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer B.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Christoffer B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas","key":"elmpau","last":"Elm","locid":"6ea1cf8e-1249-4521-a618-cb110084bd60","name":"Elm, Jonas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Wenzel","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"c838d5f7-f708-47d2-a9f4-c4c12e5c7c2d","name":"Andreasen, Jens Wenzel","orcid":"0000-0002-3145-0229","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Østergaard","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"bf44c259-9a6f-4aeb-beb3-686808f3b251","name":"Madsen, Anders Østergaard","orcid":"0000-0001-5422-8076","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Axel Rune Fredrik","key":"westerlundpau","last":"Westerlund","locid":"3a9f1ff8-6b4b-4e6a-90b2-0598b9513f5c","name":"Westerlund, Axel Rune Fredrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo Wegge","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"676e56d0-ddee-45f3-8b7f-c6734ee7e409","name":"Laursen, Bo Wegge","orcid":"0000-0002-1120-3191","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c2jm15954f","issn":["09599428","13645501"],"issn_org":["09599428"],"journal":"Journal of Materials Chemistry","pages":"4797-4805","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Journal of Materials Chemistry","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857525173"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-aef83e6f-fc0a-4215-9add-47913c77f3f6","ku-e906bf8b-b892-458c-9881-344cbdb55445"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Large area, soft crystalline thin films of N,N<sup>I</sup>,N<sup>II</sup>-trialkyltriazatriangulenium salts with homeotropic alignment of the discotic cores in a lamellar lattice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.50-036557","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"We propose a mechanism for the vertical reﬁnement of bigraphical reactive systems, based upon a mechanism for limiting observations and utilising the underlying categorical structure of bigraphs. We present a motivating example to demonstrate that the proposed notion of reﬁnement is sensible with respect to the theory of bigraphical reactive systems; and we propose a sufﬁcient condition for guaranteeing the existence of a safety-preserving vertical reﬁnement. We postulate the existence of a complimentary notion of horizontal reﬁnement for bigraphical agents, and ﬁnally we discuss the connection of this work to the general reﬁnement of Reeves and Streader","author_count":3,"contributors":["Perrone, Gian David","Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381812"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bigraphical Reactive Systems","Categorical structure","Horizontal refinement","Safety preserving","Vertical refinement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bigraphical refinement","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.55","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381812","ids":["itu-2447e78a-df0d-4859-ab59-4553e65463a2"],"keyword":["Bigraphical reactive systems","Categorical structure","Horizontal refinement","Safety-preserving","Vertical refinement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0E1C5DDB1E4BB074911CFA4C68542D5F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.55","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://eptcs.org/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://cgi.cse.unsw.edu.au/~rvg/eptcs/content.cgi?Refine2011","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gian David","key":"perronepau","last":"Perrone","name":"Perrone, Gian David","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4204/eptcs.55","issn":["20752180"],"pages":"20-36","publisher":"University of New South Wales Press","series":"Electronic Proceedings in Theoretical Computer Science. EPTCS","status":"p","title":"Electronic Proceedings in Theoretical Computer Science. EPTCS","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84965173713"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2447e78a-df0d-4859-ab59-4553e65463a2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bigraphical Refinement","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381812","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Vi præsenterer den første version af PEPL, et deklarativt Proces-orienteret, Event-baseret Programmeringssprog baseret på den fornyligt introducerede Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) Graphs model. DCR Graphs tillader specifikation, distribuerede udførsel og verifikation af pervasive event-baserede arbejds- og forretningsprocesser ved at deklarere relationer for betingelser (conditions), opfølgninger (responses) og eksludering/inkludering mellem hændelser. For at kunne danne grundlag for PEPL udvider vi DCR Graphs til at tillade 1) hændelser og relationer parameteriseret med dataværdier, 2) underprocesser der kan dannes dynamisk, og 3) specifikation af hændelser der skal udføres af computeren. Vi præsenterer PEPL-sproget og dets konstruktioner, og vi giver en reference til hvor man kan finde den første implementation af PEPL lavet i JavaScript og derfor tillader at udføre programmer at blive defineret og udført i en almindelig web-browser.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Thomas","Zanitti, Francesco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382559"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Business process modeling","DCR Graphs","Declarative programming","Event based systems","PEPL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a process oriented event based programming language","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2335484.2335530","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382559","identifier":[{"id":"84865019491","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-572706da-ddff-4c49-8635-2d25b794d0fc"],"keyword":["Business process modeling","DCR Graphs","Declarative programming","Event-based systems","PEPL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FAF528E5C6B82861B1C7782AE54C880A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=2335530","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2335484.2335530","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesco","key":"zanittipau","last":"Zanitti","name":"Zanitti, Francesco","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2335484.2335530","isbn":["9781450313155"],"pages":"377-378","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 6th ACM International Conference on Distributed Event-Based Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865019491"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-572706da-ddff-4c49-8635-2d25b794d0fc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A process-oriented event-based programming language","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382559","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"We present an extension of the recently introduced declarative process model Dynamic Condition Response Graphs ( DCR Graphs) to allow nested subgraphs and a new milestone relation between events. The extension was developed during a case study carried out jointly with our industrial partner Exformatics, a danish provider of case and workflow management systems. We formalize the semantics by giving first a map from Nested to (flat) DCR Graphs with milestones, and then extending the previously given mapping from DCR Graphs to Buchi-automata to include the milestone relation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Thomas","Mukkamala, Raghava Rao","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382921"],"event":{"end":"2011-04-22","place":"Tehran, ir","start":"2011-04-20","title":"4th International Conference on Fundamentals of Software Engineering","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Buchi Automata","Case Study with Industry Partner","Declarative process models","Milestone Relation","Nested Subgraphs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nested dynamic condition response graphs","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/34548834/fsenpaper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382921","identifier":[{"id":"84860690224","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6ef08ac6-df19-4e67-82ba-7954a4e87070"],"keyword":["Buchi-Automata","Case Study with Industry Partner","Declarative Process Models","Milestone Relation","Nested Subgraphs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DCD776E1FFAB89F167DA6CF40961A58B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/34548834/fsenpaper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-29320-7_23","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007%2F978-3-642-29320-7_23?LI=true","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raghava Rao","key":"mukkamalapau","last":"Mukkamala","name":"Mukkamala, Raghava Rao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-29320-7_23","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"343-350","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"7141"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860690224"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6ef08ac6-df19-4e67-82ba-7954a4e87070"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Nested Dynamic Condition Response Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?m